/* 9-letter-cap stories: 300 parodies, generated by tools/build-word-readers.mjs from library/word-stories.json. Do not edit. */
window.READERS.push(
  { id: "w9-004-the-bean-receipt", title: "The bean receipt", pay: 1280000, lib: 9, text: "Bo traded a banana cart for magic beans. Fern demanded a receipt. The seller had vanished, so they planted the beans beside his sign. A beanstalk rose into a cloud, taking the sign with it. Bo climbed with his tail round each stalk. A giant demanded rent. Fern showed the sign, which promised free lodging. The giant sighed. He gave them breakfast, then climbed down to change his sign." },
  { id: "w9-002-the-glass-vine", title: "The glass vine", pay: 1320000, lib: 9, text: "Nell had a splendid tail, but the glass shoe would not fit it. Bram tried every monkey in the palace. Nell asked why a tail needed a shoe. The prince had dropped it while climbing a vine. Nell took the shoe up the tree and caught rain in it. At breakfast the thirsty prince came for a drink. He found Nell beside his lost cup and asked to share her branch." },
  { id: "w9-005-the-dragon-tooth-fairy", title: "The dragon tooth fairy", pay: 1320000, lib: 9, text: "Lark put a dragon tooth under her leaf pillow. Dot warned that a terrible fairy might come. Lark stayed awake with her breakfast banana. At dawn a tiny fairy tugged at the tooth, but it weighed more than her cart. Lark looped her tail round it and helped. The fairy offered a coin. Lark asked for a brush instead. Next day she cleaned the dragon teeth. The fairy hired a larger cart." },
  { id: "w9-008-the-moat-soup", title: "The moat soup", pay: 1340000, lib: 9, text: "Otto guarded the castle moat with a splendid spear. June came to rescue the royal banana trees, but the moat smelled delicious. A witch had turned it into soup. June dipped her tail, yelped, and fetched a spoon. Otto refused to leave his post until June showed him that the post was now a carrot. They ate a path across. The king thanked them, then asked why his bridge had no gravy." },
  { id: "w9-007-the-honest-mirror", title: "The honest mirror", pay: 1360000, lib: 9, text: "Rose asked the magic mirror who had the finest tail. It said Kip, who had spilled breakfast on his. Rose called this a terrible error. The mirror showed Kip using his sticky tail to lift a trapped beetle. Rose wiped her own tail, then used it to pull a small monkey up a steep branch. That night the mirror named Rose. Kip asked who had the cleanest floor. The mirror went dark." },
  { id: "w9-028-the-gnome-hat-map", title: "The gnome hat map", pay: 1360000, lib: 9, text: "Lulu found a tiny map sewn inside a splendid hat. Moss said it led to a gnome kingdom. They followed it through roots, over a log, and under the banana stall. Lulu carefully lifted a board with her tail. Beneath it sat a gnome counting crumbs. The map was his hat lining, and he wanted it back. Lulu traded it for a tour. The kingdom had one chair. Moss had to reign while standing outside." },
  { id: "w9-011-the-frog-toll", title: "The frog toll", pay: 1380000, lib: 9, text: "Ada kissed the frog at the bridge. It stayed a frog and charged her a banana. Len said the tale promised a prince. The frog held up a contract, then pointed to the crown on its head. Ada read the fine print with her tail holding the page flat. The prince could choose his own shape. She paid for a return ticket instead. At breakfast the frog kissed her coin and hoped for gold." },
  { id: "w9-003-the-sleeping-gate", title: "The sleeping gate", pay: 1380000, lib: 9, text: "Tuck found the castle asleep, including its gate. Wren shook the bars, but they only snored. Their breakfast was inside. Tuck made a generous offer of one banana if the gate would wake. It dreamed of fruit and opened its mouth. Wren slipped through with her tail round a bar and fetched the baskets. They left a banana in the hinge. The gate woke and thought lunch had grown in its teeth." },
  { id: "w9-010-the-tiny-quest", title: "The tiny quest", pay: 1380000, lib: 9, text: "Hazel packed a splendid sword for her quest. Tom packed breakfast. The map led through dark roots to a chest no bigger than a walnut. Hazel tried to pry it open with her sword, but the blade bent. Tom used the tip of his tail. Inside lay a tiny crown and a plea to guard an ant king. Hazel stuck her bent sword in the soil as a fence. Tom fed the ants banana crumbs." },
  { id: "w9-030-the-royal-moat-ferry", title: "The royal moat ferry", pay: 1380000, lib: 9, text: "Rex rode to rescue Pia from a tower. The bridge had fallen, and his horse refused to swim. Pia carefully lowered a basket on a vine. Rex put his splendid sword inside. She sent it back with a banana and a fare sign. He climbed in, tail curled round the rope. Pia hauled him across and opened a ferry service. Rex stayed to sell tickets. The horse got a season pass and a seat with a wider door." },
  { id: "w9-042-the-chocolate-shield", title: "The chocolate shield", pay: 1400000, lib: 9, text: "Ari made a chocolate shield for the royal trial. Nola warned that the dragon had a terrible sweet tooth. Ari held the shield high as the dragon breathed fire. It melted over his tail. The dragon stopped and licked the shield instead. Nola tossed bananas into the warm pool of sweets. The judges tasted them and called the trial a draw. Ari opened a stall beside the arena. His next shield came with a spoon." },
  { id: "w9-014-the-golden-egg-pan", title: "The golden egg pan", pay: 1400000, lib: 9, text: "May found a golden egg beneath her banana tree. Orin brought a splendid pan and tried to fry it. The egg dented the pan. May tapped the shell with her tail and heard a tiny voice asking for shade. They built a nest under leaves. At breakfast a golden goose hatched and ate every banana peel. Orin sold the dented pan as a nest bowl. May kept the goose, which laid plain eggs with shiny yolks." },
  { id: "w9-009-the-borrowed-spell", title: "The borrowed spell", pay: 1400000, lib: 9, text: "Fenn borrowed a spell to clean the monkey tower. Kit read the warning, but Fenn had waved his tail. Every banana peel grew a broom. They swept the beds into the yard and the wizard into a bucket. Kit held up the splendid spell book. Fenn found the word reverse on its cover. He turned the book round. The brooms swept the beds home, then took breakfast from the table as their pay." },
  { id: "w9-071-the-lost-continent-spoon", title: "The lost continent spoon", pay: 1400000, lib: 9, text: "Ada found an ancient continent on a spoon handle. Ben packed bananas for the splendid voyage. They sailed across a pond and found a tiny island shaped like the map. Ada planted a flag with her tail. The ground shook. A turtle rose beneath them and paddled toward shore. Ben called their discovery a moving continent. Ada gave the turtle a banana peel and took down the flag. Their next map came on a plate, which stayed still." },
  { id: "w9-082-the-jungle-survey-whistle", title: "The jungle survey whistle", pay: 1400000, lib: 9, text: "Otis marked a jungle path with a splendid whistle call. Fia wrote each call on a banana leaf. A bird copied the notes from a far tree. Otis followed it and walked in a circle. Fia caught his tail before he crossed their own tracks again. She whistled a new tune. The bird copied that too. Their discovery became a bird lesson. Fia tied leaves to the path, and Otis saved his whistle for the march back home." },
  { id: "w9-027-the-phoenix-ash-tray", title: "The phoenix ash tray", pay: 1400000, lib: 9, text: "Dara bought a phoenix to warm her tree house. Wes built an enormous perch. The bird burst into flame beside the banana bowl and left a pile of ash. Dara carefully swept it into a tray with her tail. At dawn it hatched again beneath a baked banana. Wes wanted a cage. Dara set out a fresh tray instead. Soon the village lined up for hot fruit. The phoenix got a new perch and a strict closing hour." },
  { id: "w9-013-the-straw-palace", title: "The straw palace", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Nico built a palace from straw. Tess built hers from banana crates. A terrible wind blew Nico into Tess through the open door. The king ordered a stone palace by breakfast. Nico had no stone, so he tied his tail to the crates and stacked them round the throne. Tess sold tickets to watch the wind test. It blew through the gaps. The king declared fresh air a royal asset and paid them in fruit." },
  { id: "w9-026-the-snow-queen-kettle", title: "The snow queen kettle", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Una found the banana grove trapped in ice. Beck brought a splendid sword to fight the snow queen. Una brought a kettle. She poured warm water over one stem, and the fruit came loose. The queen arrived to demand silence. Her teeth shook too much for speech. Una offered tea and breakfast. Beck used his sword to stir the pot. The queen thawed the grove in return for a kettle she could carry home." },
  { id: "w9-089-the-hidden-river-hinge", title: "The hidden river hinge", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Jade traced a lost river beneath the mountain. Elm carried bananas and a splendid spade. They found a stone door that hummed with water. Jade pushed it with her tail, and the river rushed out through a narrow gap. Elm could not shut it. A crocodile floated past with the missing hinge pin in its mouth. Jade traded a banana for the pin. They fixed the door, opened it slowly, and gave the village a river with a tap." },
  { id: "w9-025-the-shadow-bridge-toll", title: "The shadow bridge toll", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Toby had to cross a bridge before breakfast. Sal, the troll guard, demanded a terrible riddle first. Toby asked what had a tail but could not climb. Sal guessed for an hour. Toby sat on the rail and peeled a banana. At last he pointed to the bridge shadow, which ended in a narrow tail. Sal leaned over to see. Toby crossed behind him. Sal charged the shadow a toll and spent all day waiting for payment." },
  { id: "w9-075-the-asteroid-pet-leash", title: "The asteroid pet leash", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Gail found treasure inside a small asteroid. Koa drilled a hole, and the rock began to roll away. Gail caught it with a leash held in her tail. Its shell cracked open to reveal a moon snail. Koa called the discovery a mining failure. Gail offered the snail banana leaves from their ship garden. It followed them home and ate the stone steps. Koa sold the smooth dust. Gail moved the leash to a very large stake." },
  { id: "w9-121-the-marathon-wrong-ribbon", title: "The marathon wrong ribbon", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Wes ran the marathon toward a splendid yellow ribbon. Nell waited by the real finish with a banana basket. Wes crossed a ribbon tied round a dangerous tree stump. It marked a hole. He fell waist deep and caught a root with his tail. Nell pulled him free. They finished last together. Wes asked to keep the ribbon as a trophy. The gardener made him fill the hole first, so his trophy came with a spade and muddy hands." },
  { id: "w9-016-the-ogre-shoe-shop", title: "The ogre shoe shop", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Sol opened a shoe shop in a hollow tree. Bea sold laces woven from strong vines. An enormous ogre asked for shoes by breakfast, but Sol had only monkey sizes. Bea looped her tail through a lace and measured the feet. Sol cut two banana boats into soles. The ogre stepped into the stream and floated off smiling. Bea put a sign on the tree offering shoes for wet days. Sol charged extra for oars." },
  { id: "w9-143-the-longest-tail-ruler", title: "The longest tail ruler", pay: 1420000, lib: 9, text: "Vera entered a longest tail contest. Kip stretched his tail along an enormous ruler. Vera beat him by one inch. A detective noticed her tail curved behind a banana crate. Inside lay a spare rope tied to its tip. Vera said the rope was a tail coat. The judge measured both tails without clothes. Kip won, then lent Vera his prize scarf. She wore it round her neck, where the rules allowed any length she liked." },
  { id: "w9-021-the-invisible-cape-peg", title: "The invisible cape peg", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Puck wore a splendid cape that made him vanish. Nia could still see his banana, floating through the hall. He ate it to hide, then dropped the peel on a guard. The guard followed the peel trail to the pantry. Puck hung the cape on a peg and asked Nia to hide him. She carefully put a bowl on his head. The guard found an empty cape and a strange bowl with a tail. He arrested the bowl." },
  { id: "w9-022-the-royal-pea-ladder", title: "The royal pea ladder", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Ava stacked eight beds above a pea to test a royal guest. Finn climbed the tower with his tail round a post. At breakfast he said he had slept badly. Ava reached for the splendid crown, but Finn pointed to a loose bed leg. It rocked all night. She fixed it with the pea. Finn slept well the next night. Ava gave him the crown for finding the fault and kept the pea under the leg." },
  { id: "w9-056-the-raft-with-brakes", title: "The raft with brakes", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Liam built a raft to reach a waterfall. Rue warned that the map showed a terrible drop. Liam tied banana crates beneath the raft and called them brakes. At the edge Rue hooked her tail round a branch. The raft swung into the bank and the crates broke. Bananas drifted over the fall. Liam climbed down to fetch them and found a quiet pool. Rue built a path to it. Their next raft trip began at the bottom." },
  { id: "w9-006-the-wish-pond-drain", title: "The wish pond drain", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Milo wished the pond would fill with bananas. It did, and Ash fell into the heap. Milo wished for a splendid boat, but it sat on top of the fruit. The pond spirit said he had one wish left. Ash poked a tail through the boat drain and pulled up a plug. Water rushed in beneath their breakfast. Milo wished for forks. They sailed home with fruit for the village and a boat full of lunch." },
  { id: "w9-038-the-spell-book-sneeze", title: "The spell book sneeze", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Alba opened the forbidden book on a splendid branch. Sid sneezed into its pages. A spell jumped out and turned the bananas blue. Alba carefully checked the index for a cure. Sid sneezed again, and the fruit turned gold. They fed one to a crow. It stayed a crow and asked for more. Alba closed the book before Sid took another breath. They sold golden fruit at the fair and used the money to buy him a cloth." },
  { id: "w9-031-the-enchanted-door-bell", title: "The enchanted door bell", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Eli reached a splendid door in the mountain. Mo rang its bell with his tail. A voice asked them to state their quest. Eli wanted the golden banana. Mo wanted breakfast. The door opened for Mo and shut in front of Eli. Mo returned with a banana on a plate. Eli called this cheating. The door said it had run a cafe for years and wished heroes would read the menu. Eli ordered toast and got a seat." },
  { id: "w9-053-the-glacier-picnic-flag", title: "The glacier picnic flag", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Polly planted a splendid flag on the glacier. Seth put their breakfast beneath it while they mapped the coast. An hour later the flag had moved. Polly accused a rival crew. Seth followed banana peels across the ice and found their flag on a seal. Polly had stuck it in a harness left by a fisher. She used her tail to untie it. They shared their last banana and mapped the seal route as a very wet road." },
  { id: "w9-073-the-pirate-silent-drum", title: "The pirate silent drum", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Milo led a raid with a splendid drum. Bea said its noise would warn the enemy. Milo wrapped banana leaves round the skin and struck it with his tail. The drum gave a soft cough. They crept across the deck, then found the enemy waiting with tea. A messenger had heard the cough and called a doctor. Milo admitted he wanted their gold. Bea bought their old coins instead. The doctor charged them for a quiet drum lesson." },
  { id: "w9-041-the-waterfall-crown", title: "The waterfall crown", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Uma found a crown behind a waterfall. Zed put it on and demanded a treasure. Water poured from the crown into his eyes. Uma read the marks inside. It belonged to the king of rain. She tied it to her tail and swung into the banana grove, where the trees had wilted. The crown watered each root. Zed became royal bucket keeper. He still wore it on feast days, with a leaf tucked over his nose." },
  { id: "w9-066-the-buried-chest-lid", title: "The buried chest lid", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Wren dug for treasure under a palm. Rex had counted nine steps from a waterfall. Their spades struck wood. Wren hooked her tail into a crack and tugged, but the lid rose with their whole camp on it. The island was a giant chest. Rex wanted to open it. Wren pointed to the tents, banana trees, and sleeping crew. They shut the lid and dug a smaller hole. Rex found a coin and agreed it was quite enough." },
  { id: "w9-018-the-sword-in-the-stump", title: "The sword in the stump", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Elm tugged the sword in the stump with both hands. Joss tried her tail. Neither could free it. A messenger said whoever pulled it out would rule the forest. Elm noticed a splendid latch beneath the bark. He opened the stump like a box. The sword fell into his lap. Joss found the old king inside, eating bananas. He had hidden there to nap. Elm shut the latch and chose a quiet branch of his own." },
  { id: "w9-020-the-dragon-library-card", title: "The dragon library card", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Ivy climbed into a dragon cave to fetch a stolen book. Mel waited outside with breakfast. The dragon curled round an enormous heap of books but could not turn a page with its claws. Ivy used her tail to hold the book open. Mel brought the banana bowl inside. The dragon lent them the book after the last page. Ivy made it a library card. Its first fine covered three scorched pages and one melted spoon." },
  { id: "w9-023-the-cave-echo-oath", title: "The cave echo oath", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Hugo swore to bring a treasure home from the cave. Mae heard the echo swear the same oath. They carried bananas through the dark. At a fork Hugo asked which way to go. His echo shouted both ways. Mae carefully tapped each wall with her tail. One wall rang like a drum. Behind it lay a chest full of bells. They took one home. The echo kept the rest and rang them whenever it felt lonely." },
  { id: "w9-068-the-volcano-bath-ticket", title: "The volcano bath ticket", pay: 1440000, lib: 9, text: "Fern climbed an enormous volcano to study its smoke. Dax packed a towel and a pineapple. They reached a warm pool, where a guard demanded bath tickets. Fern showed her science pass. The guard charged extra for steam. Dax dipped his tail and found the water cold. The smoke came from a kettle behind a rock. Fern pulled its plug. The guard refunded their fee. They ate fruit on the crater rim and watched real clouds drift past." },
  { id: "w9-019-the-pumpkin-coach-seat", title: "The pumpkin coach seat", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo needed a coach to reach the moon feast. Ned turned a pumpkin into one with a borrowed wand. It looked splendid until Cleo sat down and sank into soup. Ned read the wand label carefully. It made meals, not wheels. Cleo tied her tail to a vine, swung to the feast, and carried the pumpkin with her. The guests had brought dry bread. Her soup won the royal prize. Ned rode home in the empty rind." },
  { id: "w9-100-the-river-map-fish", title: "The river map fish", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Jem tagged a fish to map a waterfall. Ria held the splendid net with her tail. The fish swam upstream instead and returned with a banana peel. Jem called it a failed study. Ria followed it to a hidden grove above the falls. They found ripe fruit hanging over the river. Jem revised his map and released the fish. Ria left one banana on the bank each week. The fish kept the peel and ignored every new tag." },
  { id: "w9-129-the-pie-crust-disguise", title: "The pie crust disguise", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Gail entered a splendid banana pie in the fair. Rex baked a chocolate cake and hid it beneath a thin crust. The judge cut both pies. Gail saw brown crumbs on the knife and objected. Rex claimed cake was only thick pie filling. Gail wrapped her tail round the rule sheet and read it aloud. Pies needed a top and a bottom crust. Rex added a crust beneath his cake. The judge accepted it and required a much larger fork." },
  { id: "w9-099-the-pirate-deck-chessboard", title: "The pirate deck chessboard", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Ira dared a dangerous captain to play a game for his treasure. Meg painted the deck as a chess board. Waves made the pieces slide, so Ira held his king with his tail. The captain claimed this broke the rules. Meg tied every piece to the deck with fine vines. Neither player could move. Ira offered a draw and a banana meal. The captain accepted. Meg sold him the vine chess set as a perfect game for rough seas." },
  { id: "w9-049-the-fireworks-wand", title: "The fireworks wand", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Jade had to light the royal candles to earn a wizard hat. Lou handed her a fireworks wand by mistake. She pointed it at the splendid cake. Sparks burst from the bananas and chased the king under a table. Jade wrapped her tail round a wet cloth and caught each spark. Lou put them in jars. The candles stayed dark, but the jars lit the hall. Jade earned her hat. Lou earned a job cleaning the royal ceiling." },
  { id: "w9-076-the-swamp-boot-ferry", title: "The swamp boot ferry", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Pia stepped into the swamp and lost a boot. Seth pulled her out by the tail. Their splendid map said dry land lay beyond the reeds. Pia found her boot floating toward a crocodile. She threw it a banana instead. Seth tied a vine to the boot and used it as a tiny ferry for their packs. They crossed on roots. The crocodile followed the fruit to shore, where Pia traded it the other boot for safe passage." },
  { id: "w9-113-the-football-hollow-ball", title: "The football hollow ball", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Moss kicked an enormous football into the banana grove. June caught it with her tail and heard a rattle. The referee suspected a dangerous trick. Moss opened the seam and found a tiny bell. A goat had swallowed their old ball and the coach had bought a pet toy as a spare. June tied the bell to the goal post. Each score rang it. The coach kept the new rule, and the goat learned to wait beside the fence." },
  { id: "w9-077-the-planet-mirror-sale", title: "The planet mirror sale", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Nova found a planet that mirrored each move. Hal waved his tail, and a splendid monkey waved back. They offered the mirror crew bananas. The other crew offered theirs too. Nova stepped closer and hit glass. The planet was a showroom window inside a spaceship. Hal found a price tag on the frame. They bought one mirror for the ship gym. Nova logged the discovery as useful furniture. Hal trained his tail with a partner who never missed a turn." },
  { id: "w9-017-the-fairy-cake-tax", title: "The fairy cake tax", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Mina baked a cake for the fairy queen. Cobb ate its banana crown before she came. A terrible curse made his tail grow a cake at each sneeze. Mina feared a flood of frosting, but Cobb found the cakes delicious. He sneezed into empty pans until the queen arrived. She saw the bare first cake and the full table. Cobb paid her tax in cake. The queen lifted the curse because she had run out of plates." },
  { id: "w9-039-the-royal-river-fee", title: "The royal river fee", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Cato declared himself king of a puddle beneath the banana tree. Joy built an enormous dock from twigs. A terrible drought shrank the realm before breakfast. Cato ordered rain, but the sky ignored him. Joy carried a bowl of water in her tail and poured it into the puddle. Cato named her royal river. She charged him one banana per bowl. By sunset he gave her the crown and went to fetch water from the pond." },
  { id: "w9-054-the-jungle-map-napkin", title: "The jungle map napkin", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Toma found a map to an ancient treasure on a cafe napkin. Eden packed a pineapple and a coil of vine. They climbed trees for three days before the marks led them back to the cafe. Toma held the napkin against the window with his tail. The map was a stain from spilled soup. Eden peeled the fruit beside the cook. Beneath its rind lay a gold ring the cook had lost. Toma claimed the soup had been right." },
  { id: "w9-040-the-giant-pocket-maze", title: "The giant pocket maze", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Koa entered an enormous maze to find Elsie. He tied a vine round his tail and left bananas at each turn. A hungry giant ate the fruit trail. Koa heard Elsie call from above. The maze lined a pocket worn by the giant, and she had climbed a seam. Koa carefully followed her voice. They escaped through a button hole. The giant found a vine in his pocket and hung his keys on it, ending the maze for good." },
  { id: "w9-063-the-canyon-rope-choir", title: "The canyon rope choir", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Nell had to cross a canyon with a messenger bag. Remy tied a splendid rope between two banana trees. Nell walked onto it, tail high for balance, and heard a low note. Wind played the rope like a string. Remy tightened it until the tune rose. Nell sang along and crossed in time with the beats. They left the rope there. Each new traveler paid a banana to join the song. Remy bought ear plugs with the first fee." },
  { id: "w9-057-the-alien-tail-socket", title: "The alien tail socket", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Mara met an alien beside her banana tree. Gus offered it a splendid meal. It pointed at their tails, then at an empty socket on its spaceship. Mara refused to plug herself in. Gus stuck a vine into the hole. Lights blinked, and the ship rose one inch. The alien gave them a fruit tree in thanks. Mara planted it far from the house. When it grew, each branch had a socket. Gus bought very long cords." },
  { id: "w9-096-the-sea-monster-dentist", title: "The sea monster dentist", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Cato sailed into an enormous mouth while seeking a treasure island. Orla stopped the boat with her tail round a tooth. The sea beast groaned. A pineapple had wedged beneath its tongue. Cato pushed the fruit loose with an oar. The beast spat them toward shore, then followed for more care. Orla opened a dockside tooth clinic. Cato sold soft banana meals. The beast paid with pearls and kept its mouth shut whenever a boat needed a quiet crossing." },
  { id: "w9-052-the-pirate-compass-cough", title: "The pirate compass cough", pay: 1460000, lib: 9, text: "Kira stole a compass from an enormous pirate ship. Abe hid it in a banana jar. The needle pointed toward the jar lid instead of north. Kira shook it and heard a cough. A tiny messenger sat inside, trying to breathe. She opened the case with her tail. He had been hired to point toward gold but wanted shore leave. Kira sailed where he asked. His home was a bank. She returned the compass and opened an account." },
  { id: "w9-093-the-robot-stowaway-mouse", title: "The robot stowaway mouse", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Nia built a robot to guard their spaceship. Wes found a mouse eating the banana stores. The robot refused to catch it because it wore a splendid crew badge made from foil. Nia took the badge with her tail. The robot chased her instead. Wes made a new badge for Nia and marked the mouse as a guest. The robot brought it one crumb each day. Nia locked the stores and hired the mouse to test the door gaps." },
  { id: "w9-139-the-domino-courtroom", title: "The domino courtroom", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Rose and Evan argued over a domino game at the splendid banana cafe. Rose said his tail had moved a tile. Evan claimed the table shook. They took the board to a courtroom made of crates. The judge tested the table and spilled its pineapple drink. One leg rested on a loose peel. Rose removed the peel. Evan replaced the tile. They finished the game while the judge charged them a drink fee and ate the peel as evidence." },
  { id: "w9-043-the-dangerous-lullaby", title: "The dangerous lullaby", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Bryn learned a dangerous song that put foes to sleep. Flo plugged her ears with banana bits and guarded him at the castle. Bryn sang at the gate. The guards slept, but so did his splendid horse. It lay across the path. Flo tied her tail round the gate latch and hauled it open. Bryn hummed in his own sleep. Flo dragged him home in a cart and made him practice with the song book shut." },
  { id: "w9-088-the-alien-grammar-gift", title: "The alien grammar gift", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Dara gave an alien a splendid speech box. Remy tested it by asking for a banana. The box replied that he was a banana. The alien carried him toward its spaceship pantry. Dara grabbed his tail and changed the box dial. Now it said he owned a banana. The alien bowed and offered a fruit basket as tribute. Remy left the dial there until Dara asked for her share. He learned the word ours before they ate the basket." },
  { id: "w9-001-the-crown-that-peeled", title: "The crown that peeled", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Pip drew the gold crown from a stone and found a banana stuck beneath it. Moss bowed. The monkeys in the trees bowed too, until Pip bit the fruit. The crown slipped over his eyes. A terrible dragon had stolen their breakfast, Moss said. Pip could hear the dragon snore behind the stone. He fed it the peel, which made it sneeze up six baskets of fruit. Pip gave back the crown. A king should see his lunch." },
  { id: "w9-047-the-dungeon-orchestra", title: "The dungeon orchestra", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Vera heard an orchestra beneath the castle. Ben said the terrible king had locked up the players. They climbed down using their tails and found six guards banging spoons on banana bowls. A rat had stolen their keys, and the noise kept it away from their lunch. Vera played a soft tune on a reed. The rat came to listen. Ben took the keys from its nest. The guards hired the rat to turn their sheet music." },
  { id: "w9-132-the-archery-target-wheel", title: "The archery target wheel", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Jade shot arrows at a splendid target in the banana grove. Otto moved it on a wheel to save her a walk. A dangerous gust sent the wheel downhill. Jade dropped her bow and hooked her tail round its axle. Otto caught her hands. They hauled the target back to flat ground. The arrows pointed toward every tree they had passed. Jade used them to mark a walking course. Otto locked the wheel and waited for her final shot." },
  { id: "w9-148-the-rope-ball-reading-hour", title: "The rope ball reading hour", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo wanted rope ball beneath the splendid banana tree. Tom preferred a quiet reading seat. Their committee met on its branches. Cleo tied the ball rope to her tail and showed how little room it needed. Tom ducked as it swept his book away. The committee split the day into play hours and quiet hours. Cleo retrieved the book. Tom built a seat above the ball reach. Each took a banana break when the other hour began." },
  { id: "w9-012-the-hood-with-pockets", title: "The hood with pockets", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Red wore a hood with enormous pockets to carry bananas to Gus. A wolf asked which tree held her grandpa. Red gave it a map upside down. It ran straight into a pond. When she reached Gus, her pockets shook. The wet wolf had climbed from the pond and hidden in one. Gus offered it breakfast on the porch while Red stitched both pockets shut. The wolf went home with a full belly and a map it could finally read." },
  { id: "w9-044-the-messenger-goose", title: "The messenger goose", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Etta hired a messenger goose to call Gil to the palace. The goose ate her splendid seal and swallowed the note. Gil found it honking beside his banana tree. Etta arrived on foot, tail full of spare paper. She offered the goose a bowl of water. It coughed the note into the bowl, where the ink ran. Gil guessed that the queen wanted soup. He brought a pot. She had wanted supper, so he got a royal job." },
  { id: "w9-092-the-pirate-anchor-orchard", title: "The pirate anchor orchard", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Lulu dropped an enormous anchor to hide from a dangerous pirate. Dax climbed the mast with his tail and saw the foe pass. When they tried to leave, the anchor would not rise. It had hooked a sunken banana tree from the harbor garden. Lulu cut the chain and tied a buoy to it. She sold maps to the sunken orchard. Dax led tours in a glass boat. The pirate came back, bought a ticket, and forgot the chase." },
  { id: "w9-173-the-contract-tiny-print-leaf", title: "The contract tiny print leaf", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Ari signed a contract to buy an entire banana grove. Meg read the tiny print with a detective lens. It covered a grove painted on a leaf. Ari held the leaf in his tail and demanded real fruit. The seller offered a painted banana. Meg took the leaf to the art market. A buyer paid twice the grove price for its detail. Ari accepted, then bought one actual tree. Meg checked the roots before letting him reach for the pen." },
  { id: "w9-034-the-knight-laundry-flag", title: "The knight laundry flag", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Lio tied a splendid flag to his lance and rode toward the foe. Nan noticed it was her bedsheet. She chased him through the banana grove, holding his tail to slow him. A messenger met them at the border and mistook the sheet for a peace flag. Both armies stopped to talk. Nan demanded soap before any treaty. The generals washed her sheet in the stream. Lio went home with peace and a lance full of wet socks." },
  { id: "w9-137-the-detective-bridge-squeak", title: "The detective bridge squeak", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Orla heard a squeak each night from the splendid bridge. Poe hired a detective before the noise spoiled breakfast. Orla hung below the bridge by her tail and watched the joints. A loose bolt moved when the banana cart rolled across. Poe had blamed mice. They tightened the bolt and found a mouse family asleep beneath it. Orla left them a quiet leaf bed. Poe paid the detective for the wrench he had brought, rather than the mouse trap." },
  { id: "w9-037-the-royal-dungeon-window", title: "The royal dungeon window", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Ira got locked in a dungeon for eating royal bananas. Hope brought an enormous file hidden in breakfast. Ira used it on the bars until his tail ached. Then Hope noticed the window had no glass, only thin bars across the lower half. Ira climbed over them and dropped into the garden. He returned the file to the cook. The king ordered higher bars. Hope planted a banana tree beneath them and sent Ira a ladder bill." },
  { id: "w9-060-the-cave-of-lost-hats", title: "The cave of lost hats", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Evan entered a cave to seek buried treasure. Sol carried a lantern and a banana lunch. The ceiling dripped on their hats, which stuck fast when they looked up. The discovery was a cave full of honey. Sol climbed his shoulders and used her tail to peel each hat free. They carried one sticky hat home. The village bees followed it. Evan sold honey by the spoon and hired Sol to keep the cave map away from bears." },
  { id: "w9-106-the-tennis-tail-knot", title: "The tennis tail knot", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Fern played tennis with her splendid tail round the racket. Lou claimed she had two hands free and an unfair edge. The referee tied their hands behind them. Lou tried to use his tail too, but he had tied it in a knot to hold a pineapple snack. Fern waited while he untied it. They played a long match, then split the fruit. The referee made a new rule allowing snacks only between games, with tails fully untied." },
  { id: "w9-033-the-unicorn-mud-bath", title: "The unicorn mud bath", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Arlo sought a unicorn in the grove. Meg found hoof marks beside the banana pond. A splendid horn poked from the mud, but its owner refused to rise. It had spent yesterday posing for royal coins and wanted a rest. Arlo cleaned the horn with his tail while Meg held a towel. The unicorn let them ride home on one condition. They had to splash through every puddle. The royal painter met them at the gate and fainted." },
  { id: "w9-154-the-marketing-hollow-fruit", title: "The marketing hollow fruit", pay: 1480000, lib: 9, text: "Etta sold a banana with no pulp as a premium light snack. Gus counted earnings while customers found only peels. The marketing team claimed air was the new fruit. Etta tried to show it with her tail holding a peel open. A customer blew through it like a horn. Soon the shop rang with protests in loud notes. Gus refunded every sale. Etta renamed the stock party horns. This time she showed the empty center before taking any coins." },
  { id: "w9-045-the-beautiful-mud-shoe", title: "The beautiful mud shoe", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Lena bought a spell to make her shoes beautiful. Otis spilled mud on them before the royal ball. She rubbed the shoes with her tail, but they began to sing. The witch had enchanted the mud instead. Lena went to the ball barefoot, carrying the shoes in a basket. The splendid court band lost its tune. Her shoes sang the right notes. The prince asked for a dance, then hired her basket for the rest of the night." },
  { id: "w9-046-the-pineapple-prophecy", title: "The pineapple prophecy", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Remy found a prophecy carved in a pineapple. Sia read that the king would fall when the fruit was ripe. They rushed to the splendid throne with their tails linked for speed. The king reached for the fruit and slid off his chair. Its leg had broken. Remy caught him while Sia fixed the chair with a stone. They ate the prophecy. The king ordered softer fruit for the next royal warning and a chair with four sound legs." },
  { id: "w9-142-the-hoop-that-turned-flat", title: "The hoop that turned flat", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Uma threw balls through a splendid hoop tied to a banana tree. Dex set an enormous prize basket below it. A dangerous wind turned the hoop flat. Uma tossed the ball high, but it rested on the rim. Dex climbed with his tail round the branch and tilted the hoop. The ball fell through onto the prizes. Uma won a squashed banana. They moved the hoop lower, tied its frame tight, and ate the prize before testing it again." },
  { id: "w9-158-the-committee-empty-cup", title: "The committee empty cup", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Ira sought funds for a banana stand. Meg chaired the committee and offered drinks. Every cup was empty because the budget had cut water. Ira held his cup in his tail and asked for rain instead. The committee approved a rain study, hired a weather clerk, and bought an enormous cloud chart. Meg looked at the cost. Ira opened the window during a shower. Their cups filled for free. Meg cancelled the study and funded a roof for the stand." },
  { id: "w9-029-the-cursed-spoon-choir", title: "The cursed spoon choir", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Jem stole a spoon from the witch kitchen. It sang whenever he tried to eat breakfast. Ora warned that a terrible curse could last forever. Jem tied the spoon to his tail and climbed to the grove. Each time he scooped banana mash, the song shook ripe fruit from the branches. Ora fetched baskets. By noon the witch came to reclaim it. Jem offered her half the crop. She left the spoon and asked for the tune." },
  { id: "w9-079-the-cave-lantern-refund", title: "The cave lantern refund", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Cobb bought a splendid lantern for his cave trip. Una bought bananas. In the cave the lantern went dark. Cobb shook it, and a firefly crawled out demanding breakfast. Una gave it fruit, but it flew away. She traced the wall with her tail until they reached daylight. Cobb took the lantern back to the shop. The seller offered fresh fireflies. Una asked for a candle. Cobb got a refund, which the firefly tried to eat through his pocket." },
  { id: "w9-095-the-moon-passport-peel", title: "The moon passport peel", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Alba reached the moon border without her passport. Finn had used it to wrap bananas. The guard demanded a splendid seal before their spaceship could land. Alba curled her tail round the paper and pressed the fruit flat. Its brown marks looked like a face. The guard compared them with Finn and waved him through. Alba had to wait. Finn sent back a fresh passport with a banana stamp. The guard smiled and admitted her for the fruit festival." },
  { id: "w9-122-the-detective-empty-box", title: "The detective empty box", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Zia wrapped an enormous box for Pip. At breakfast it stood empty under the tree. Pip hired a detective to find the gift. Zia saw a trail of ribbon up a branch. Her gift was a hammock, and a bird had used its loose strings to haul it into a nest. Pip climbed with his tail round the branch and lowered it. The bird kept the wrapping. Pip napped in his hammock while the detective billed him for one tree climb." },
  { id: "w9-105-the-cake-contest-clue", title: "The cake contest clue", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Etta entered a chocolate cake in the village contest. Seth tasted a splendid slice before judging began. Someone had swapped the cake for banana mud. Etta found tiny claw marks in the icing. She followed them with her tail sweeping dust away. A squirrel had dragged the real cake under the stage. Seth lifted the boards. Etta served the untouched half and won for flavor. The squirrel kept the mud cake, which made a fine wall around its nuts." },
  { id: "w9-124-the-spelling-bee-hive", title: "The spelling bee hive", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Bryn entered a spelling bee beside the banana grove. Kit carried an enormous word book. Bryn spelled beehive, and a swarm rose from the next tree. Kit held the book above them with her tail. The judge asked for butterfly. Bryn refused to speak. Kit showed that the swarm had moved because the lunch cart hit its branch. Bryn finished the word. No butterfly came. He won a ribbon, which Kit tied to the cart as a warning flag." },
  { id: "w9-048-the-forgotten-sunrise", title: "The forgotten sunrise", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Esme had forgotten where she hid the sun after her magic show. Cal searched the cupboard with a candle. The banana grove had gone dark. Esme shook her splendid hat, but only socks fell out. Cal felt warmth under the table. He lifted the cloth with his tail and found the sun inside a melon bowl. Esme set it free through the window. The whole village woke late, except the baker, who had baked by the bowl." },
  { id: "w9-061-the-submarine-soup-leak", title: "The submarine soup leak", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Bea took a submarine below the reef. Otto packed banana soup in an enormous flask. A leak sent bubbles past the window, and Bea ordered him to seal it. Otto poured soup into the crack. A crab plugged the hole with its claw to catch the meal. Bea rose toward shore while Otto fed the crab through the crack. They bought it a bowl before it let go. The repair shop charged them for one shell and two soups." },
  { id: "w9-062-the-time-machine-lunch-bell", title: "The time machine lunch bell", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Kit built a time machine from a splendid clock he bought yesterday and a banana crate. Aya climbed in with her tail round the bell. They meant to see next year, but the machine stopped at lunch. Kit tried again. Lunch again. Aya read the dial. He had bought a kitchen timer. They sold rides to hungry monkeys, each ending beside a full bowl. Kit never reached next year, but he knew the exact minute the cook served every meal." },
  { id: "w9-067-the-comet-umbrella", title: "The comet umbrella", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo opened an umbrella to shield their spaceship from a comet. Joss said space had no rain. A shower of tiny stones hit the splendid cloth. Cleo held its handle with her tail while Joss steered. The cloth tore, but the ribs caught a shining stone. At home the museum bought it. Joss bought Cleo a new umbrella. She opened it indoors to check the ribs. A second stone dropped into the banana bowl and paid for their next trip." },
  { id: "w9-090-the-comet-souvenir-stall", title: "The comet souvenir stall", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Mina opened a souvenir stall on a comet. Cal built an enormous counter from banana crates. The comet circled the sun before any guests arrived. Mina tied her tail to the stall and waited through another orbit. Cal finally put a sign on the spaceship lane. Guests came, but each wanted a postcard sent home. Mina used the crates as mail bins. Cal sold the empty counter as a comet relic. Their new shop had stamps and no waiting room." },
  { id: "w9-097-the-explorer-boot-museum", title: "The explorer boot museum", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Hope dug up a splendid boot beneath the banana grove. Zia called it evidence of an ancient king. Hope brushed it with her tail and found yesterday written inside. The village cobbler had thrown it out after a leak. Zia had already sold museum tickets. Hope filled the boot with water to show why the king had lost it. Guests liked the display. The cobbler opened a repair booth next door and bought every ticket holder a dry sock." },
  { id: "w9-131-the-detective-shell-phone", title: "The detective shell phone", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Ivy installed a shell phone in her detective office. Sol called to report a stolen banana. She heard only waves. Sol had spoken into a shell by the pond, not a phone. Ivy followed his wet tracks and found him beside an enormous basket. His banana lay beneath the lid. She lifted it with her tail. Sol paid her fee in fruit. Ivy kept the shell on her desk because its quiet waves helped her think between real cases." },
  { id: "w9-299-the-composer-final-banana", title: "The composer final banana", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo could not finish the orchestra song. Poe, the musician, waited with an enormous banana basket. Cleo tried a loud ending, then a soft one. Neither fit. Poe peeled a banana with his tail and dropped the skin into a bin. Its soft tap matched the last beat. Cleo wrote one simple note and stopped. The audience heard the finished song that night. Poe brought no basket on stage, only a small drum for the note a peel had taught them." },
  { id: "w9-091-the-cave-guide-hat-light", title: "The cave guide hat light", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Bram sold cave tours using a splendid light on his hat. Sia brought bananas for the guests. A low ceiling knocked the hat into a stream. Bram followed its glow and left the group behind him. Sia stretched her tail across the path to keep them still. She heard a waterfall ahead and called Bram back. He hired her as guide. The hat drifted into the gift shop below, where it sold for more than the tour had earned." },
  { id: "w9-098-the-spaceship-curtain-sail", title: "The spaceship curtain sail", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Nan lost the spaceship engine near a dusty planet. Poe hung an enormous curtain outside to catch sunlight. The ship drifted toward a dangerous cloud of rocks. Nan wrapped her tail round the curtain rope and tilted it. They sailed between the stones and reached a repair dock. Poe sold the curtain as a solar sail. Nan bought a fresh engine and new curtains. She kept one rope tied to her seat because the sun did not charge for fuel." },
  { id: "w9-149-the-treasure-hunt-shoelace", title: "The treasure hunt shoelace", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Dara followed clues to a treasure beneath the banana tree. Sol raced ahead with an enormous shovel. His shoelace caught a root, and he fell beside the last clue. Dara pulled him up with her tail. A chocolate coin lay inside a tiny box. Sol wanted half for finding the hole. Dara gave him half for digging it, then ate hers. They filled the hole together. The teacher added a final clue asking hunters to leave the tree roots safe." },
  { id: "w9-104-the-pumpkin-bowling-lane", title: "The pumpkin bowling lane", pay: 1500000, lib: 9, text: "Dax made a bowling lane from smooth banana trunks. Meg brought an enormous pumpkin as her ball. It rolled once and split in half. Dax counted no points. Meg put each half on her feet and slid down the lane, tail held high. The pins fell. The referee called this a dangerous new sport. Dax rebuilt the lane as a slide and charged a peel per ride. Meg kept the seeds to grow fresh foot cups for next season." },
  { id: "w9-035-the-wand-warranty", title: "The wand warranty", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Gail bought a wand that promised splendid spells. Poe used it to turn banana peels into shoes. The shoes walked away without them. Gail carefully read the warranty. It covered spells only while the wand was dry. Poe had dipped it in soup. Gail wrapped her tail round the shoes and pulled them back. They put the wand in the sun. Once dry, it turned the shoes into peels. Poe wore leaves home and kept the receipt." },
  { id: "w9-153-the-courtroom-peel-oath", title: "The courtroom peel oath", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Dex brought a banana peel to the courtroom as proof of a fall. Ivy asked him to swear the peel had caused it. He placed a hand on the contract and his tail on the peel. Down he went. Ivy objected that the court floor had caused this second fall. The judge sealed the peel in a jar and awarded Dex a mop. Ivy appealed for a safer oath table. The judge moved it beside the sink and made them both wash." },
  { id: "w9-050-the-crocodile-moat-lease", title: "The crocodile moat lease", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Tia leased the moat to a crocodile who promised to guard the palace. Evan planted banana trees along the bank. The splendid beast ate the fruit and let every guest across its back. Tia read the lease aloud. It had agreed to guard the palace from hunger. Evan laughed, but Tia asked for the rent. The beast opened its mouth and showed a gold coin beneath its tongue. They paid a dentist to fetch it and kept the tenant." },
  { id: "w9-103-the-missing-race-whistle", title: "The missing race whistle", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Cal lost the whistle for the banana race. Ivy searched each enormous basket. A sharp note came from a tree, then another from the table for the judges. Cal followed both and found nothing. Ivy curled her tail round a branch and spotted a bird with the whistle. It dropped the whistle into the soft cake at breakfast. Cal blew it, but only crumbs came out. Ivy clapped to start the race. The bird won the crumb cleanup without a whistle." },
  { id: "w9-107-the-library-footprint-pie", title: "The library footprint pie", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Gil found muddy prints leading to a splendid library shelf. Vera said someone had stolen the cookbook. Gil dusted the marks with flour held in his tail. They formed a trail to the kitchen. The cook had taken the book to make a pineapple pie but dropped it behind the oven. Vera retrieved it with a hook. Gil ate pie while the cook cleaned the marks. He returned the book with one new page showing how to wash library floors." },
  { id: "w9-169-the-political-leaf-fence", title: "The political leaf fence", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Uma drew a political border through the banana grove. Cal built a fence from leaves. Each monkey had to pay a crossing fee to reach the water. A gardener moved the water bucket to each side in turn, using his tail as a handle. Uma taxed the bucket. Cal objected that the official map showed only land. The gardener planted the bucket on the border. Uma and Cal argued until thirst made them share it. The leaves dried and blew away." },
  { id: "w9-102-the-pancake-high-jump", title: "The pancake high jump", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Bo trained for the high jump on a splendid banana branch. Nola cooked pancakes beneath him. Each time he jumped, she raised a pancake on a fork. Bo cleared the bar and landed beside breakfast. At the meet he stopped halfway because no pancake waited below. Nola waved the fork from the finish mat. He sailed over the bar and ate his prize. The judges measured the jump, then ordered Nola to lower the fork before the next event." },
  { id: "w9-164-the-courtroom-banana-scale", title: "The courtroom banana scale", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Orla weighed court evidence on a balance. Rex put a banana on one side and his contract on the other. The fruit pulled the scale down. He claimed this proved the debt too heavy. The courtroom judge asked him to eat the banana. Rex peeled it with his tail and took a bite. The scale balanced. Orla wrote that he had paid in fruit. Rex kept the peel as a receipt, which the clerk required him to dry before filing." },
  { id: "w9-072-the-space-helmet-orchard", title: "The space helmet orchard", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Zed cracked his helmet beside the spaceship. Joy had one spare, but it held an enormous banana seedling. She moved the plant into a pot while Zed held his breath. Its roots clung to the glass. Joy used her tail to ease them free. Zed put on the helmet and breathed the scent of wet soil. Back home he planted the seedling in the yard. Joy kept the cracked helmet as a dome and grew herbs beneath it." },
  { id: "w9-078-the-captain-salt-chart", title: "The captain salt chart", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Arlo drew a chart in salt on the deck. May warned that a dangerous wave would erase it. He built an enormous fence round the chart and tied his tail to the mast. The sea stayed calm, but a crew member spilled soup. Salt ran into every port mark. May tasted the soup and found it good. She sold bowls to the crew while Arlo drew a new chart on cloth. He marked the soup stall as their safest harbor." },
  { id: "w9-083-the-moon-dust-bakery", title: "The moon dust bakery", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Ava tested moon dust inside the spaceship oven. Gil had hidden banana dough there for supper. The mixture rose into an enormous loaf that filled the cabin. Ava pushed it away with her tail while Gil opened the vent. The loaf squeezed out like a soft comet. They followed it down to the moon and cut slices. Ava wrote that moon dust helped bread rise. Gil wrote that the oven needed a lock and a much clearer meal schedule." },
  { id: "w9-116-the-vault-snack-bag", title: "The vault snack bag", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Polly carried a splendid vault pole to the meet. Remy used it to hang the team bananas. When Polly ran, her tail caught the snack bag. She rose with fruit swinging below and landed past the mat. A dangerous landing, said the judge. Remy moved the mat farther out. Polly tried again without the bag and fell short. They lowered the bar and counted her safe jump. Remy served bananas only after every pole stood in the rack." },
  { id: "w9-101-the-detective-peel-clock", title: "The detective peel clock", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Ada found a banana peel beside the broken clock. Rex called a detective. She measured the peel with her tail, then checked the enormous clock hands. One hand smelled of fruit. Rex admitted he had used it to reach lunch on a high shelf. Ada fitted it back and wound the clock. It ran twelve minutes fast. Rex offered to climb up and fix it. Ada moved the bananas lower and made him keep both feet on the floor." },
  { id: "w9-123-the-pudding-relay-baton", title: "The pudding relay baton", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Ari brought a pudding cup instead of a baton to the relay. Dot called this a dangerous mistake. He ran his lap with the cup balanced on his tail. Dot took it and sped beneath the banana trees. The splendid pudding spilled at each turn. Their team finished with an empty cup. The judges gave them no medal, but every runner asked for the recipe. Ari sold it to the cafe and bought a proper baton with the first coins." },
  { id: "w9-141-the-detective-flour-moon", title: "The detective flour moon", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Tess saw a splendid white moon mark on the banana shed. Bram called the detective because the lock was broken. Tess found flour inside the mark. She curled her tail round the latch and opened the door. The baker stood within, covered in dough. He had slipped against the wall and broken the lock while seeking his breakfast fruit. Bram gave him a key and a bill. Tess washed the moon away before the village started a hunt for ghosts." },
  { id: "w9-032-the-gingerbread-repair", title: "The gingerbread repair", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Bess found a splendid cottage whose sweet cake wall had a crack. Hal bit the loose edge. The witch charged him for damage. Bess used her tail to spread banana paste in the crack and carefully pressed the piece back. Hal offered to mend the roof. The witch handed him a bag of sweets and watched every bite. By dusk the cottage stood firm. Hal paid for one window he had eaten. Bess earned a room with a plain wooden door." },
  { id: "w9-065-the-robot-peel-judge", title: "The robot peel judge", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Pax built a robot to sort bananas. Mina wrote a splendid rule that ripe fruit went left. The robot put every banana left, then put Pax there too. His yellow coat matched its chart. Mina tried to pull him free with her tail, but the robot sorted her coat beside him. Pax called this a dangerous flaw. Mina took off both coats. The robot folded them into the peel bin. They fed it a new chart and kept their coats." },
  { id: "w9-118-the-singing-prize-silence", title: "The singing prize silence", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Sal practiced a splendid song for the contest. Uma watched from a tree, holding a banana in her tail. On stage Sal lost his voice. Uma held her tail behind his back and tapped the beat. He waved his hands to show the song instead. The audience copied each move. A messenger brought him the prize for best silent act. Sal took a sip of water and thanked them aloud. The judge asked if he could keep the thanks silent too." },
  { id: "w9-130-the-skating-pond-ticket", title: "The skating pond ticket", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Hugo trained on an enormous frozen pond. Aya sold seats on the bank and served pineapple cubes. At noon the ice softened. Hugo used his tail to hold a low branch while Aya pulled his skates free. The crowd demanded their money back. Aya rolled the benches to a shaded pond that still had firm ice. Hugo skated a short show there. He bowed from the bank this time. Aya kept one cube on the ice as a warning test." },
  { id: "w9-166-the-campaign-soup-spoon", title: "The campaign soup spoon", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Rose promised a spoon for every monkey in her campaign. Dax ordered spoons from a corporate supplier. The town had no soup bowls. Rose served banana mash on leaves, but the spoons tore them. Dax held a leaf flat with his tail while Rose tried again. The town voted her out and kept the spoons. She opened a bowl stall across from the council. Dax handled orders. Every new policy lunch brought her more trade than the campaign ever had." },
  { id: "w9-183-the-courtroom-soft-gavel", title: "The courtroom soft gavel", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Koa made a courtroom gavel from a banana. Rue warned that the official bench needed a firmer tool. Koa struck it once, splashing the witness book. The court laughed, and the witness forgot his lines. Rue wiped the book with her tail and asked him to speak plainly. He admitted the story was false. Koa kept the soft gavel for nervous guests but used a wooden one for rulings. Rue kept a cloth beneath both and no fruit near the ink." },
  { id: "w9-232-the-historical-royal-queue", title: "The historical royal queue", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Ira crowned Tom during an ancient ceremony beneath the banana trees. The enormous crown slid over his ears. A messenger called the next prince, and Tom refused to move. Ira lifted the crown with her tail and found the kings were only in a practice pageant. Tom had taken the script as a real order. Ira gave him a paper crown to keep. He joined the queue again and waited for his cue, which now came with a clear practice sign." },
  { id: "w9-110-the-slowest-sprint-medal", title: "The slowest sprint medal", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Jem entered the sprint with an enormous lunch basket. Ria said it would slow him down. Jem tied his tail round its handle and ran anyway. Halfway through, the lead runner stopped with a cramped leg. Jem shared a banana, then helped him walk. Everyone passed them. Ria gave Jem the kindness medal at breakfast. Jem hung it on his basket. At the next race the whole team brought snacks, and no one wanted to leave him behind." },
  { id: "w9-133-the-marble-mayor-race", title: "The marble mayor race", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Koa entered the marble race to choose the school mayor. Mina polished an enormous marble until it shone. Koa picked a small chipped one and nudged it with his tail. Mina rolled ahead but got stuck in a narrow groove. Koa went past and won. At breakfast he ordered wider grooves for everyone. Mina used her marble as a tool to smooth the track. Koa made her parks chief and promised to leave polishing out of the next race." },
  { id: "w9-024-the-witch-broom-parking", title: "The witch broom parking", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Zia landed her broom in the royal banana tree. Rufus found three more brooms jammed beside it. The witches had come for a splendid feast but could not fly home. Zia carefully looped her tail round a branch and climbed to the top. She tied each broom to a leaf tag, then called its owner by name. Rufus held the ladder. Last came the queen, who had parked her broom upside down and lost her hat in the roots." },
  { id: "w9-251-the-broadcast-banana-desk", title: "The broadcast banana desk", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Ada read the broadcast news from a banana crate. Rex, the director, ordered a taller desk to look serious. Ada stacked crates until only her ears showed. Rex raised the camera. Her tail knocked the top crate, spilling fruit into view. Viewers sent notes praising the honest farm report. Ada lowered the desk and reported actual banana prices. Rex kept one tall crate for weather maps, but he nailed it to the floor before letting anyone forecast a gust." },
  { id: "w9-111-the-locked-banana-locker", title: "The locked banana locker", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Kip locked his bananas in an enormous locker. Nia heard him shout when they vanished. A detective checked the latch and found no mark. Nia pushed her tail through the vent and touched a cold plate. Kip had locked the fruit in the school oven by mistake. The cook had moved it before baking bread. He returned a tray of warm bananas. Kip ate them, then painted his real locker blue so hunger would not guide him wrong again." },
  { id: "w9-134-the-stolen-rain-gauge", title: "The stolen rain gauge", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Lark lost the rain gauge from her splendid garden. Tuck offered his detective badge. They found banana peels beside the empty post. Tuck suspected the cook, but Lark followed drops up a tree with her tail brushing leaves aside. A monkey gardener had borrowed the gauge as a flower vase. He thought it measured stem height. Lark took it back and gave him a jar. Tuck solved the next case by asking before he dusted the whole garden for prints." },
  { id: "w9-163-the-council-tail-census", title: "The council tail census", pay: 1520000, lib: 9, text: "Nan ran a census by counting tails in the banana grove. Gus filed the official total. A committee found the town had doubled overnight. Nan had counted each tail once going up a tree and once coming down. Gus proposed two votes per citizen to match the ledger. Nan crossed out the spare count instead. She marked each monkey hand with washable ink. Gus tried to get a second mark on his foot. Nan gave him a mop and one vote." },
  { id: "w9-120-the-contest-jar-frog", title: "The contest jar frog", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Vera filled a splendid jar with banana chips for a guessing contest. Len counted them through the glass. At breakfast the count had changed. Vera searched for a thief and found a frog inside the jar. It had climbed in through the loose lid and eaten chips. Len caught it with his tail and set it by the pond. Vera counted the chips again. Len won the prize by guessing fewer. The frog entered no guess but kept its free meal." },
  { id: "w9-125-the-muddy-medal-mold", title: "The muddy medal mold", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo won a splendid gold medal, but Bram found mud inside it. A detective checked the podium. The medal maker had used clay to save gold and forgotten to bake it. Cleo wrapped the wet medal in banana leaves with her tail. She took it back and asked for one that would last. The maker fired the clay and painted it gold. Bram called it cheap. Cleo hung it proudly because it still marked the race she had won." },
  { id: "w9-085-the-robot-moon-garden", title: "The robot moon garden", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Rose sent a robot to plant an enormous grove on the moon. Dex gave it banana seeds and a shovel. When they arrived, the robot had planted the shovel in neat soil. A spaceship brought more seeds, but the robot buried its ramp too. Rose tied her tail round the control lever and held it still. Dex changed the task to dig, then plant seeds. The grove grew. The robot kept watering the shovel until Rose gave it a flower pot." },
  { id: "w9-152-the-branch-office-root-fee", title: "The branch office root fee", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Cal opened a branch office high in the banana tree. Nia handled the contract with the root owner. Cal promised efficient service because clients could swing straight in. The first client climbed the trunk and asked for a chair. Cal offered a branch. Nia used her tail to hold the client steady through the meeting. The root owner charged rent for each handhold. Cal moved the office to the ground and kept the branch address on his letters for prestige." },
  { id: "w9-161-the-ownership-banana-shadow", title: "The ownership banana shadow", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Lark sold Sid ownership of a banana tree shadow. Sid held meetings beneath it and charged rent. At noon the shadow shrank, leaving his clients in the sun. Lark said the contract promised a shadow, not a fixed size. Sid used his tail to hang a cloth from the tree. The new shade covered all his seats. Lark demanded cloth rent. Sid pointed to the sky. He owned the shadow, and the cloth had only made it wider. Lark sat outside." },
  { id: "w9-146-the-missing-trophy-echo", title: "The missing trophy echo", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Ari lost the splendid singing trophy from the banana hall. Rue searched with her detective lens. Each tap on the wall gave a bright ring. Ari had hung the trophy inside the drum to make his last song louder. He opened the drum with his tail and found it wedged against the skin. Rue loosened the frame. The trophy came free, but the drum sounded dull. Ari thanked her with a quiet song and kept the prize on a shelf." },
  { id: "w9-114-the-science-fair-rain-hat", title: "The science fair rain hat", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Ned built a rain hat for the science fair. Bea brought an enormous watering can to test it. Water ran off the brim and soaked his tail. Ned claimed the invention worked because his ears stayed dry. Bea tested it beside the banana plants. The brim watered a full ring of roots. Ned changed his sign from rain hat to garden tool. He won second prize and a watering can. Bea bought the hat for dry ears on wet days." },
  { id: "w9-189-the-insurance-scarecrow-suit", title: "The insurance scarecrow suit", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Rose dressed a scarecrow in her official insurance suit to guard bananas. Bo saw it and filed a claim for a broken branch. Rose explained that straw could not approve payment. Bo asked why it wore the badge. She took the badge back with her tail and checked his branch. Wind had broken it, as his contract covered. Rose paid the claim. Bo gave the scarecrow a plain hat. Birds returned, so Rose hired Bo to guard fruit in plain clothes." },
  { id: "w9-259-the-composer-banana-metronome", title: "The composer banana metronome", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Ira composed a song with a banana swinging as a metronome. Len, the musician, played beneath the tree. The fruit ripened and swung more slowly. Ira blamed Len for losing the beat. He caught the banana with his tail and showed the soft stem. Ira fetched a clock, but its ticking spoiled the song. Len tapped a steady beat on the trunk instead. Ira wrote it down before the fruit fell. They ate the old metronome and practiced with a plain wooden weight." },
  { id: "w9-126-the-fishing-contest-hat", title: "The fishing contest hat", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Dara cast her line toward an enormous fish. Finn cast his toward her splendid hat. He caught it and reeled her off the bank. Dara grabbed a banana root with her tail and stayed dry. The fish took her bait while she freed the hook. Finn offered his pineapple lunch as an apology. Dara used its leaves to repair her hat. The judge counted no fish for either monkey, but gave Finn a warning for fishing above the water." },
  { id: "w9-127-the-detective-ink-tail", title: "The detective ink tail", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Esme found a forged note asking for ten bananas. Bo called the detective and locked the splendid fruit room. The note had a long ink smear. Esme compared it with each monkey tail, then noticed her own black tip. She had written a shopping list while painting the fence and forgotten to sign it. Bo opened the fruit room. Esme washed her tail before writing the next list. The detective charged one banana for the ink stain on his desk." },
  { id: "w9-136-the-costume-contest-fern", title: "The costume contest fern", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Nan dressed as a fern for the contest. Remy wore a dangerous dragon mask. Nan stood so still that a gardener tried to water her. She wrapped her tail round his can and asked for a pause. Remy laughed, then sneezed smoke from banana flour hidden in the mask. The judge gave Nan best costume and Remy best sneeze. Nan went home in plain clothes. Remy kept sneezing until the gardener washed the flour from his nose with the prize can." },
  { id: "w9-184-the-permanent-temporary-stall", title: "The permanent temporary stall", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Lark opened a temporary banana stall. Dex stamped its contract for one day. Each dawn she took it apart and rebuilt it, calling the stall new. The permit office sent a secretary to watch. Lark used her tail to lift the roof, but the secretary counted the same roots beneath it. Dex offered a permanent permit for less than a week of daily fees. Lark bought it and left the roof up. The secretary bought fruit and finally got a dry seat." },
  { id: "w9-256-the-rehearsal-royal-sneeze", title: "The rehearsal royal sneeze", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Fern practiced a royal death in rehearsal. Sid arranged costumes beneath the banana stage. Fern lay still, but dust from the crown made her sneeze. The audience of helpers laughed. Sid cleaned the crown and wrapped its lining in a leaf. Fern died quietly on the next run. The director missed the sneeze and asked for it back. Fern changed the play to a royal nap. Sid wrote one sneeze into the script and kept the dusty crown locked away." },
  { id: "w9-277-the-animation-uphill-lunch", title: "The animation uphill lunch", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Dara drew an animation of a banana rolling uphill. Len, the director, said the movement broke physics. Dara added a monkey tail pushing it from behind the rock. Len approved, but the tail belonged to no visible actor. Dara drew a hungry monkey on the next frame. The audience now saw a plan rather than a mistake. The monkey reached the summit and ate the fruit. Len kept the final close view, where the tail rested and the hill no longer mattered." },
  { id: "w9-084-the-waterfall-rope-receipt", title: "The waterfall rope receipt", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Tia rented a rope to cross a waterfall. Mo read the contract while she tested its splendid knots. Halfway across, a bell rang on the bank. Their rent had expired. Tia hooked her tail round the rope and stayed put while Mo argued. The owner demanded another banana. Mo rolled one across the rope to Tia, who ate it and threw back the peel. The owner slipped into his own safety net. Mo took the receipt and extended the lease." },
  { id: "w9-145-the-sled-race-sand-hill", title: "The sled race sand hill", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Zia waited for snow to test her splendid sled. Ned pointed to the sand hill beyond the banana grove. She tied her tail round the sled rail and slid down. Sand piled at its nose and stopped her halfway. Ned brought an enormous board to spread the weight. The next run reached the bottom. They held a race at breakfast. The winner got a banana, while Zia kept a jar of sand to prove her winter sport needed no winter." },
  { id: "w9-213-the-spy-dinner-spoon", title: "The spy dinner spoon", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Mina brought a secret listening spoon to dinner with Rex. He discussed the stolen banana plans while stirring soup. The spoon sent each slurp to an enormous speaker outside. Guards rushed in, fearing a dangerous beast. Mina slipped the spoon into her tail and pointed at the soup pot. Rex admitted he had hidden the plans beneath it. The guards took the plans back. Mina ate with a plain spoon afterward, though the speaker still echoed one last noisy gulp." },
  { id: "w9-058-the-desert-snow-cart", title: "The desert snow cart", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Dune pushed an enormous cart of snow into the desert. Cora said they should have brought water. Dune claimed the snow would save their banana crop at the distant camp. By noon the cart held a puddle. Cora carefully bent her tail round the drain plug and held it shut. They reached camp with warm water and a wet map. Dune planted the banana shoots. Cora kept the cart to carry shade cloth, which weighed much less than snow." },
  { id: "w9-135-the-climbing-trophy-ribbon", title: "The climbing trophy ribbon", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Meg raced Gus up an enormous tree. The trophy hung beneath a splendid banana bunch. Gus reached it first, but his tail snagged the ribbon and tied him to the branch. Meg climbed up and freed him. She carried the trophy down while he carried the fruit. The judge could not tell who had won. Meg proposed a shared prize. Gus accepted on condition that the ribbon stayed on the ground. They used it to mark a safer finish line." },
  { id: "w9-191-the-promotion-ladder-toll", title: "The promotion ladder toll", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Tess climbed an office ladder for her promotion. Poe charged a banana toll on each rung. Tess paid until she reached the official top, where a secretary asked for the final fee. Tess had no fruit left. She swung down by her tail and gathered fallen bananas beneath the ladder. Poe called them company property. Tess asked why he had dropped each payment. He returned her fees. She bought a plain ladder and climbed to a different office with lunch intact." },
  { id: "w9-208-the-history-mural-snack", title: "The history mural snack", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Hope painted the founding battle on an enormous wall. Lou posed with a spear and banana shield. A messenger brought news that the battle had never happened. The founders had argued over fruit, then shared it. Hope lowered her brush. Lou used his tail to turn the shield into a tray. Hope painted the meal instead, with the spear holding a canopy. The council approved the mural. Lou asked for a fresh banana shield because standing through history had made him hungry." },
  { id: "w9-210-the-love-letter-ink-frog", title: "The love letter ink frog", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Jade wrote Kip a beautiful letter beside the pond. A frog jumped into the ink and hopped across the page. Kip read its marks as a terrible storm warning and packed a boat with bananas. Jade met him at the dock, her tail holding the stained letter. She explained the frog. Kip unpacked the boat except for one picnic basket. They rowed to a quiet island. The frog rode in the empty ink cup and left its next letter on a plain rock." },
  { id: "w9-255-the-cinematic-banana-chase", title: "The cinematic banana chase", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Etta planned a cinematic chase through the banana market. Gus, the director, wanted a real cart crash. Etta tied the cart to her tail and stopped it before the fruit stall. Gus said nothing exciting happened. She filmed the stop close up, with bananas falling toward the lens. The audience gasped at the safe scene. Gus approved the cut. Etta returned every banana to the seller and billed the film for the bruised one she had eaten between takes." },
  { id: "w9-263-the-spotlight-banana-crown", title: "The spotlight banana crown", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Mina wore a banana crown beneath the spotlight. Rex designed the costumes for a serious royal play. A monkey in the audience smelled ripe fruit and asked for a slice. Mina kept speaking, but Rex lowered a curtain with his tail. He replaced the crown with painted wood and served the fruit during the break. The audience returned calmer. Mina finished the speech without a snack request. Rex made the next royal feast from wooden bowls, though the actors ate real food afterward." },
  { id: "w9-059-the-captain-cork-eye", title: "The captain cork eye", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Patch wore a cork over one eye to look like a dangerous pirate. Lila steered their splendid boat while he posed on the bow. He could not see the reef. Lila wrapped her tail round his waist and pulled him down before they struck it. The cork fell into a leak and stopped the water. Patch left it there. At port the crew asked about his pirate mark. He pointed at the deck and said his eye guarded the ship." },
  { id: "w9-087-the-desert-shadow-tent", title: "The desert shadow tent", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Hugo lost his tent in an enormous sandstorm. Flo stretched banana leaves across their packs to make shade. Hugo chased the tent shadow he saw on a dune, but it moved with him. Flo caught his tail and made him sit. The shadow came from their own rescue balloon. She waved a leaf. The pilot lowered a ladder and served pineapple juice on the way home. Hugo kept the leaf roof. His next tent had a bright rope tied to it." },
  { id: "w9-160-the-secretary-lunch-gate", title: "The secretary lunch gate", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Koa hired Vera as secretary for his banana firm. Her official task was keeping visitors from his lunch. Vera tied her tail across the door and asked each guest to book a time. Sales fell because no clients got through. Koa demanded an efficient plan. Vera booked him a lunch hour and served bananas only during that hour. Clients returned. Koa tried to eat during a meeting, but Vera booked the banana for noon and sent it back to wait." },
  { id: "w9-170-the-testimony-parrot-clerk", title: "The testimony parrot clerk", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Vera gave testimony about a stolen banana. Bram, the court clerk, wrote it down while a parrot repeated every word. The judge asked for a second witness. The parrot spoke, and Bram recorded it as another vote. Vera used her tail to draw a cloth over its cage. It repeated nothing. Bram realized both accounts came from her. The official record kept one witness. The judge hired the parrot to announce lunch, then regretted it when lunch was called twelve times." },
  { id: "w9-217-the-ballroom-mistaken-mirror", title: "The ballroom mistaken mirror", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Rose met a beautiful dancer in the ballroom mirror. Gus stood behind her with a splendid banana bouquet, trying to speak. Rose practiced her greeting at the glass until he thought she loved her own image. He left the bouquet on a chair. Rose saw him go and caught his sleeve with her tail. She had been too shy to turn around. Gus admitted the same. They danced facing each other. The mirror watched alone, showing the empty bouquet chair." },
  { id: "w9-070-the-satellite-tree-swing", title: "The satellite tree swing", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Lou put a satellite above the banana grove. Dara used an enormous vine to anchor its shell. Each orbit pulled the vine across the trees and swept fruit into their baskets. Lou called it a science mission. Dara used her tail to release one knot before the roots came loose. The satellite flew free, taking their basket with it. Lou sent a second craft to fetch lunch. Dara picked the next crop by hand and charged him for the launch." },
  { id: "w9-074-the-frozen-mast-flag", title: "The frozen mast flag", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Elsie sailed north to see the midnight sun. Tom tied bananas to the mast so they would not freeze on deck. They froze on the mast instead, making an enormous yellow flag. Elsie carefully chipped one free with a spoon held in her tail. The flag cracked and dropped fruit into the soup pot. A passing ship hailed their strange banner. Tom sold it hot banana soup. Elsie watched the sun while counting the coins in her warm mittens." },
  { id: "w9-080-the-star-chart-blanket", title: "The star chart blanket", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Etta stitched a star chart into an enormous blanket. Pax spread it over the spaceship controls to choose their route. He sneezed, moved three stars, and sent them toward the laundry moon. Etta pinned the cloth down with her tail. The laundry crew cleaned their dusty suits and pressed the chart flat. Pax found the right route at last. Etta charged him a banana for the trip. He paid two and asked her to stitch a compass on his sleeve." },
  { id: "w9-081-the-pirate-cork-parade", title: "The pirate cork parade", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Ned blocked the harbor with an enormous chain. Ria wanted to sell bananas across the bay. She tied corks to each bunch and floated them under the chain, steering with her tail from a small raft. Ned called this a dangerous breach. Ria offered him a cork fee. He accepted, then found every boat copying her fruit rafts. By dusk the chain guarded an empty harbor. Ned sold it to Ria, who used it to anchor her new floating shop." },
  { id: "w9-128-the-obstacle-course-tea", title: "The obstacle course tea", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Fia built an enormous obstacle course through the banana grove. Cal carried tea to the judges at its far end. He climbed the wall, crossed the ropes, and used his tail to steady each cup. The judges gave him a splendid time score. Cal said he had not entered. Fia handed him a medal at breakfast. He wore it on his tea tray. When the racers asked his secret, he told them hot tea made falling a very poor choice." },
  { id: "w9-218-the-siege-ladder-supper", title: "The siege ladder supper", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Sia led an enormous siege ladder toward the castle. Hal carried banana soup for the troops. A messenger shouted that the gates were open for supper. Sia refused to drop her ladder after carrying it all day. Hal used his tail to turn it sideways and set bowls on its rungs. They entered with a long serving tray. The castle guard thanked them for the feast. Sia accepted a peace ribbon and asked for a cart before moving the ladder home." },
  { id: "w9-233-the-beautiful-storm-bouquet", title: "The beautiful storm bouquet", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Jade brought Bo a beautiful bouquet through a terrible storm. Rain stripped every flower, leaving bare stems. She tucked the stems in her tail and climbed to his banana porch. Bo had built a vase large enough for the planned gift. Jade spoke with one word, sorry. Bo filled the vase with warm tea and put the stems in a pot. They drank while planting them. By spring the porch bloomed. Jade brought a small cup on the next wet visit instead." },
  { id: "w9-015-the-lost-tower-lift", title: "The lost tower lift", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Fia waited atop a tower with a basket of bananas. Reed called for her to lower her tail. She had spent yesterday tying it into a splendid braid, so she lowered the basket instead. Reed climbed inside. Halfway up, he sneezed and shook the rope. Fia lowered him again and sent down a note asking for stairs. Reed built them from tree limbs. They ate on the first step. Fia untied her braid so the birds could take its loose ribbons." },
  { id: "w9-055-the-moon-cheese-crater", title: "The moon cheese crater", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Nova landed on the moon and found an enormous wedge of cheese. Finn called the discovery home, then tried to plant a flag. The pole sank to its base. Nova looped her tail round it and pulled him out of a soft crater. They laid banana leaves over the hole to spread their weight. Finn took one cheese sample. Back home it melted in his pocket. Nova sold the stained flag as proof that space travel required better lunches." },
  { id: "w9-064-the-pirate-weather-spoon", title: "The pirate weather spoon", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Tess stirred her tea with a spoon that foretold storms. Bo hung it beside the banana mast. It rattled all night, so they stayed in port. Each day it warned of dangerous seas, though the bay looked splendid. Tess caught Bo tapping it with his tail. He feared sailing because he could not swim. She taught him in the shallows. The spoon fell silent. On their first voyage it bent in a real gale and stirred soup very badly." },
  { id: "w9-265-the-cinematic-cardboard-ocean", title: "The cinematic cardboard ocean", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Orla built a cinematic ocean from blue cardboard. Sid, the director, floated banana boats on its flat waves. An actor stepped through the sheet and got stuck. Orla caught his tail and pulled him back. Sid liked the dramatic whirlpool, but Orla refused another fall. She filmed a toy boat sinking into a safe bowl instead. The audience believed the storm. Orla folded the ocean into storage, and Sid paid for a real railing around every hole before the next scene." },
  { id: "w9-094-the-mountain-echo-radio", title: "The mountain echo radio", pay: 1540000, lib: 9, text: "Tuck called for help from a mountain ledge. Vera heard his voice through her splendid radio. Each reply came twice, so she thought two monkeys were trapped. Tuck threw a banana peel down to mark his spot. Vera climbed up with a rope held in her tail. She found one monkey and a deep echo cave. Their discovery drew singers from every valley. Tuck sold seats on the ledge. Vera kept the radio for real rescue calls and charged for echoes." },
  { id: "w9-112-the-kite-contest-anchor", title: "The kite contest anchor", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Lena flew a splendid kite shaped like a banana. Gus tied a pineapple to its tail for balance. The kite never left the ground. Lena cut the string holding the pineapple with a shell and gave the fruit to the judges. Her kite rose above the trees. Gus held the loose string in his own tail and ran beneath it. The judges awarded best flight and best snack to different monkeys. Gus asked for another prize for carrying the heaviest kite tail." },
  { id: "w9-138-the-leapfrog-finish-spoon", title: "The leapfrog finish spoon", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Pia played leapfrog across an enormous field. Sid placed a splendid spoon at the finish to mark the breakfast prize. Pia jumped over him with her tail curled high. He jumped over her and landed on the spoon. It flipped banana mash onto his nose. Pia stopped to laugh, so Sid crossed first. He demanded the prize. The judge pointed at his nose. Sid ate it, then shared the bowl with Pia and planted a flag at the next finish." },
  { id: "w9-262-the-orchestra-page-bird", title: "The orchestra page bird", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Lark hired a bird to turn pages for the orchestra. Gus sat in the audience with banana chips. The bird flew toward his snack halfway through the score. Lark turned the page with her tail while playing one note with her hand. Gus shared a chip and sent the bird back. Lark gave it a seed after each correct page. The concert ended in tune. Gus kept the chip bag closed, and the bird got a written menu clipped beside the music." },
  { id: "w9-109-the-garden-badge-thief", title: "The garden badge thief", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Ira wore a detective badge in the banana grove. Flo lost her splendid garden prize and asked him to find it. Ira quizzed every monkey except himself. Flo noticed his badge had green paint under its gold foil. He had borrowed her prize for his costume. Ira peeled the foil off with his tail and gave it back. Flo charged him one hour of weeding. He solved his next case wearing a paper badge with his own name on it." },
  { id: "w9-144-the-recipe-relay-lock", title: "The recipe relay lock", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Wren locked the secret recipe in an enormous tin before the cooking relay. Cal carried it to the next team with his tail round the handle. He lost the key under a banana root. Wren had to bake from memory. Her chocolate loaf rose crookedly, but it tasted rich. Cal found the key after judging ended. The tin held only a blank sheet. Wren had forgotten to write the recipe. Cal wrote it down while they ate the winning loaf." },
  { id: "w9-239-the-beautiful-duel-cake", title: "The beautiful duel cake", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Pia and Gus agreed to a duel for a beautiful poet. Each brought an enormous banana cake as a weapon because the poet loved sweets. Pia lifted hers with her tail. Gus dropped his before the first strike. The poet caught a slice and asked why they planned to waste dinner. Pia lowered her cake. They shared it beneath a tree while the poet read a new verse about foolish feasts. Gus baked a second cake as an apology and carried it with both hands." },
  { id: "w9-275-the-cinematic-royal-puddle", title: "The cinematic royal puddle", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Bea filmed a cinematic ship battle in a puddle. Hal, the director, wanted an enormous wave. He dropped a banana crate into the water. Both toy ships sank, and the camera got wet. Bea wiped the lens with her tail and built a slow wave using a flat board. Hal filmed close to the surface. The audience believed it was an ocean. Bea returned the toys to their owner. Hal kept the board and left every heavy crate far from the next puddle." },
  { id: "w9-177-the-marketing-perfect-bruise", title: "The marketing perfect bruise", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Esme sold bruised bananas under a marketing plan called soft gold. Gil counted earnings from each crate. A customer asked for firm fruit. Esme pointed to the premium shelf, where the same bananas cost twice as much. Gil lifted a bunch with his tail and revealed the bruise beneath the label. The customer bought one at the old price. Esme peeled the rest and made mash. Gil sold it honestly as soft food. The labels became lids for the mash cups." },
  { id: "w9-181-the-secretary-open-door", title: "The secretary open door", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Ivy announced an open door policy at the banana firm. Lou, her secretary, removed every office door. Wind scattered the contracts through the trees. Ivy climbed after them with her tail wrapped round a branch. A corporate visitor walked into the pantry and ate her lunch. Lou said access had improved. Ivy rehung the doors and set one hour for visits. Lou put that hour on a sign. The visitor returned at noon, carrying a banana to replace the one he ate." },
  { id: "w9-287-the-animation-lost-shadow", title: "The animation lost shadow", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Nan made an animation in which a monkey climbed a banana tree. Bo drew the shadow beside the enormous trunk. Halfway up, the shadow climbed into a different tree. Nan asked the director to choose one source of light. Bo pinned a lamp guide beneath the paper with his tail. The shadow followed the monkey correctly. Nan kept the stray version for a dream scene. The audience saw both, but the dream began with closed eyes and ended before the real climb resumed." },
  { id: "w9-147-the-juggling-contest-soup", title: "The juggling contest soup", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Bess juggled bananas at the splendid fair. Hal entered with an enormous soup pot. He tossed it once, caught it with his tail, and spilled soup over the stage. Bess slipped but caught every banana before landing. The judge called the act dangerous and stopped the show. Hal mopped the boards. Bess put her fruit in bowls and served it with his soup. Their booth earned enough to buy Hal three small juggling balls that held nothing wet." },
  { id: "w9-162-the-permanent-acting-chief", title: "The permanent acting chief", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Mina became acting chief while Tom took a banana break. Her promotion lasted six months because he never returned from the grove. The official board wanted a permanent chief but could not dismiss a monkey on break. Mina carried the lunch bell up the tree in her tail. Tom came down to eat. The board thanked him for returning and ended his leave. Mina kept her job. Tom got a new role timing breaks, with his own bell far from the fruit." },
  { id: "w9-167-the-warranty-tail-elevator", title: "The warranty tail elevator", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Sia installed an elevator in her tree office. Hal signed the warranty before checking its size. It carried one banana at a time. Sia tried to ride with her tail outside, and the door refused to close. A secretary sent their lunch up fruit by fruit while Hal climbed the trunk. The supplier said the lift met all terms because the contract promised a small lift. Sia moved it to the pantry. Hal wrote his next order while standing beside a ruler." },
  { id: "w9-176-the-committee-banana-minutes", title: "The committee banana minutes", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Dara recorded minutes for the banana committee. Pax asked why one hour of meetings filled twelve pages. Dara had written every sixty seconds as a separate event. Pax used his tail to turn the heavy stack. The official archive had room for one shelf. Dara cut the record to decisions, but there had been none. She filed a blank page. Pax proposed ending the meeting on time. Dara wrote that down and closed the book before anyone could discuss it." },
  { id: "w9-179-the-election-banana-ink", title: "The election banana ink", pay: 1560000, lib: 9, text: "Gail printed ballots with banana ink for the official election. Bo dried them across branches. Rain washed away every candidate name. The committee still wanted voting by dusk. Gail used her tail to pin plain leaves beside the box and asked voters to write a name. Bo counted them aloud. One leaf voted for rain. Gail set it aside, then found twelve more. The town elected a gardener who promised a roof over the next ballot line. Rain got no office." },
  { id: "w9-036-the-mermaid-branch-seat", title: "The mermaid branch seat", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Ria heard a mermaid asking for a seat in the banana tree. Dax built a splendid swing above the pool. The mermaid offered a pearl but could not reach the swing. Ria carefully lowered it with her tail until it skimmed the water. Dax pushed from the bank. The pearl rolled into the mud. Ria left it there. Each day the mermaid brought fish for Dax and songs for Ria. Ria gave her bananas in return and lowered the swing for each meal." },
  { id: "w9-151-the-banana-forecast-fan", title: "The banana forecast fan", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Ada presented a forecast for the banana firm. Bo set an electric fan behind her chart to cool the board. The paper rose with every gust, making sales seem steep. Ada held it down with her tail. The committee frowned at the flat line. Bo turned the fan higher. Ada unplugged it and opened the sales ledger. The firm had sold one fan and no bananas. The board voted to pivot into fans. Ada billed them for the chart paper." },
  { id: "w9-214-the-beautiful-duel-rose", title: "The beautiful duel rose", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Nan sent Sid a beautiful rose. He mistook its sharp thorns for a dangerous duel challenge and arrived with an enormous sword. Nan held the rose in her tail and asked for a vase. Sid planted his sword in the soil as a stake. They tied the rose to it and watered the roots. His rival arrived expecting a duel. Nan handed him a watering can too. The three spent the afternoon fixing the garden, and Sid left his sword where the rose needed it." },
  { id: "w9-257-the-animation-missing-peel", title: "The animation missing peel", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Gail drew an animation of a monkey slipping on a banana peel. Tom checked each frame for the director. The peel vanished halfway through, leaving the monkey falling on clean ground. Gail curled her tail round the pencil and drew it back in. Tom added a frame of a cleaner catching the falling monkey. The monkey landed safely in the next drawing. Gail liked the new scene better. Their film became a short tale about catching mistakes, and the cleaner got the biggest applause." },
  { id: "w9-194-the-budget-empty-fountain", title: "The budget empty fountain", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Wren cut the water budget for the official fountain. Bo filled its bowl with bananas to honor the saving. Citizens ate the display, leaving an enormous empty bowl. A committee praised the cheap monument. Wren sat inside it with her tail curled round the drain and heard rain begin. The bowl filled. Bo sold the collected water to nearby gardens. Wren restored a small water budget and moved the banana stall beside the fountain. The monument finally served more than a speech." },
  { id: "w9-283-the-spotlight-curtain-knot", title: "The spotlight curtain knot", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Jade opened the curtain for the spotlight scene. Sid had tied its rope to an enormous banana basket to keep it taut. Jade pulled with her tail, lifting fruit above the audience. One banana fell into a lap. The director paused the show while Sid lowered the basket. Jade replaced it with a plain weight. The scene began again. The lucky viewer kept the fruit, but Sid moved the rest to the lobby and sold them only after the curtain closed." },
  { id: "w9-182-the-forecast-weather-debt", title: "The forecast weather debt", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Jade borrowed against the banana harvest due next year. Cal wrote a forecast promising sunshine. The committee spent the coins on a marble fountain. A drought came, and the harvest shrank. Jade used her tail to clear the fountain drain. Its bowl held enough water to save the driest trees. Cal revised his report to claim the fountain was a farm tool. Jade sold its marble lions and paid the debt. The fountain stayed, with plain pipes and no forecast pinned above it." },
  { id: "w9-222-the-ancient-royal-umbrella", title: "The ancient royal umbrella", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Wren carried an ancient umbrella above the king. Gus guarded the enormous banana cart behind them. A messenger warned of rain, but the umbrella had holes shaped like royal stars. Wren used her tail to spread a plain leaf beneath it. The king stayed dry and praised the stars for good weather. Gus pointed to the dripping leaf. Wren lowered it so the king could see. He ordered plain umbrellas for everyone and kept the star one indoors above a dry chair." },
  { id: "w9-202-the-general-pineapple-cannon", title: "The general pineapple cannon", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Bo loaded a pineapple into the army cannon. Vera wanted a warning shot across the enormous enemy camp. Bo pulled the cord with his tail. The fruit landed in the enemy soup pot and splashed every officer. They waved white spoons and asked for the recipe. Vera crossed the field with salt and bananas. Both armies ate beneath one tent. Bo sold the cannon to a farm for launching seed. Vera kept the spoons as medals and retired before the next meal." },
  { id: "w9-282-the-meal-after-the-final-note", title: "The meal after the final note", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Ira wrote a rest into the orchestra score. Cal placed bananas beside each musician to fill the pause. The audience heard peeling during the silence. Ira lifted her tail to stop the noise, but everyone chewed more softly instead. Cal moved the fruit backstage. The next rest stayed quiet. After the final note Ira lowered her arm, and the players rushed for lunch. Cal wrote a meal break after the score so no one had to guess whether a rest meant food." },
  { id: "w9-284-the-recording-copy-cat", title: "The recording copy cat", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Koa heard a second voice in her recording. Len, the musician, blamed an enormous echo in the banana studio. Koa moved blankets around the walls with her tail. The voice remained. A cat sat behind the mixer, meowing each time she sang a high note. Len gave it a bed in the lobby. Koa sang alone and missed the strange harmony. She recorded one short cat chorus on its own. Len credited the cat, which accepted its fee in fish rather than fruit." },
  { id: "w9-108-the-diving-board-banana", title: "The diving board banana", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Hope polished an enormous diving board for the meet. Pax ate his breakfast banana at its far end. The peel slid beneath his feet and sent him into the pool. Hope held up a splendid score card. Pax said he had not meant to dive. She asked him to do it again. He tied his tail round a rail and placed the peel under one foot. The board bent, then bounced him high. Pax won the meet and lost his lunch." },
  { id: "w9-140-the-chalk-race-raincoat", title: "The chalk race raincoat", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Sia drew lanes for the race with splendid blue chalk. Len brought an enormous raincoat to cover them overnight. At breakfast he lifted it by the sleeves. The chalk stuck to its lining. Sia had no time to redraw every lane. She laid the coat flat, opened its buttons, and made the runners follow its blue stripes. Len used his tail to hold one corner. The race ended beside the pocket, where Sia had hidden bananas for the winners." },
  { id: "w9-207-the-ballroom-tail-fan", title: "The ballroom tail fan", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Gail carried a beautiful fan to the banana ball. Rex read its motions as secret love signs. When she opened it, he bowed. When she closed it, he fled. Gail used her tail to catch his sleeve. She was hot, not proposing marriage. Rex confessed he had studied a splendid guide to fan speech. Gail lent him the fan to cool down. They danced after he stopped reading it. The guide spent the evening propping open a window that actually needed air." },
  { id: "w9-230-the-dangerous-proposal-bridge", title: "The dangerous proposal bridge", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Gail planned to propose on a dangerous rope bridge. Kip carried an enormous banana cake across it. The bridge swayed when Gail knelt. Kip caught her tail and asked her to stand. She offered the ring halfway upright. He accepted, then proposed moving the cake to shore. They crossed holding hands and ate beneath a tree. Gail kept the bridge ticket beside the ring box. Kip kept a firm bench for every later romantic speech, with enough space for the cake too." },
  { id: "w9-264-the-recording-door-squeak", title: "The recording door squeak", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Nan wanted silence for her recording. Bo oiled every door in the banana studio. One still squeaked because his tail pressed its hinge each time he entered. Nan recorded the squeak alone and asked him to repeat it in rhythm. The musician used it as a sharp beat beneath her song. Bo got a sound credit. He moved his tail before opening the door afterward. Nan kept the squeak file, but the studio finally had quiet when she asked for it." },
  { id: "w9-294-the-recording-crate-echo", title: "The recording crate echo", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Vera wanted an echo in her recording. Cal built a tunnel from banana crates beside the studio. Vera sang into it while Cal held the far end with his tail. The echo sounded thin because the crates had enormous gaps. Cal lined them with dry leaves and tried again. The sound grew warm. The musician liked it better than a machine effect. Vera kept the tunnel for one song, then returned the crates before the grower needed them for a real harvest." },
  { id: "w9-286-the-rehearsal-audience-mirror", title: "The rehearsal audience mirror", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Mina practiced to a mirror during rehearsal. Rex arranged an enormous banana basket as her pretend audience. She bowed, saw her image bow back, and started the speech again. Rex covered the mirror with his tail holding a cloth. Mina finished without waiting for a reply. The director gave her a real audience that night. They clapped after her final line. Mina bowed once and left. Rex uncovered the mirror only after she went backstage, where a second bow could not restart the play." },
  { id: "w9-168-the-inventory-empty-shelf", title: "The inventory empty shelf", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Tess praised the banana shop for selling all its inventory. Poe pointed to the empty shelf. Their earnings report showed no cash because a loose hinge had tipped every bunch into the street. Tess saw customers gathering fruit below. She climbed down with her tail round the rail and set up a stall beside the pile. Poe fixed the hinge. Tess sold the last banana and filed a corrected report. The shelf stayed empty, but this time the cash box did not." },
  { id: "w9-198-the-official-queue-vine", title: "The official queue vine", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo installed an official queue vine at the permit desk. Sid held it with his tail to keep monkeys in line. A committee praised the smooth system. Then the vine grew overnight, carrying the queue round three trees and through the banana stall. Guests arrived with full baskets and blank forms. Cleo cut the vine to desk length. Sid planted the spare section in a garden. Its fruit paid for a second clerk, which shortened the queue better than any knot had." },
  { id: "w9-292-the-orchestra-final-cough", title: "The orchestra final cough", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Tess warned the orchestra audience not to cough during the quiet song. Len, the musician, swallowed a banana chip and felt a cough rising. He held it until his face turned red. Tess noticed and stopped the music with her tail raised. Len coughed safely and drank water. The audience joined him in one enormous burst. Tess gave them a pause, then began again. The quiet song stayed quiet because no one had to pretend breathing was less important than the score." },
  { id: "w9-150-the-fastest-soup-waiter", title: "The fastest soup waiter", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Elm entered a speed contest with an enormous tray of banana soup. Mina warned that the judges wanted running, not serving. Elm balanced the tray on his tail and sped along the track. Each judge took a bowl as he passed. By the finish his tray was empty, but the clock showed a record. The committee argued over whether soup helped him run. Mina offered a second trial. Elm brought empty bowls and won again, though the judges liked the first race better." },
  { id: "w9-204-the-beautiful-balcony-bucket", title: "The beautiful balcony bucket", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Dex sang beneath Rose and her beautiful balcony. Rose lowered a bucket for his love note. He put a banana inside because his hands shook too much to write. Rose peeled it and sent the bucket back with seeds. Dex planted them beside the splendid wall. Weeks later vines reached the balcony. He climbed with his tail round the stems. Rose met him halfway, carrying a watering can. They wrote their first note together on a leaf asking the gardener for a wider pot." },
  { id: "w9-280-the-filmmaker-snack-sequel", title: "The filmmaker snack sequel", pay: 1580000, lib: 9, text: "Gail made a film about one stolen banana. Rex, the filmmaker, demanded a sequel with an enormous bunch. Gail wrote a chase, but every actor stopped to eat the props. Rex wanted more action. Gail filmed the meal and the argument over who should wash the bowls. The audience laughed at the new ending. Rex asked for a third film. Gail wrapped her tail round the empty basket and said the next story needed fruit first. He bought a bunch and hired a prop guard." },
  { id: "w9-201-the-dangerous-wedding-ladder", title: "The dangerous wedding ladder", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Ada climbed a dangerous ladder to rescue Gil before his arranged wedding. He sat in the banana tower wearing a splendid coat. Ada hooked her tail round the sill and asked him to jump. Gil said he wanted the wedding but feared the stairs. Ada lowered the ladder into the hall. He climbed down one rung at a time and thanked her. The bride met them with cake. Ada stayed to hold the ladder while the priest fetched his hat from the tower." },
  { id: "w9-231-the-secret-agent-hammock", title: "The secret agent hammock", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Hope watched a dangerous spy from an enormous banana branch. Lou sold hammocks below. Hope hid in one with her tail round the rope and waited for the secret exchange. Lou rocked the hammock to attract buyers. Hope fell asleep. The spy bought a hammock. His stolen packet fell into the display one as he lifted his purchase. Hope woke on the evidence. She returned the packet to court. Lou charged for the nap, and Hope ordered a chair for every future watch." },
  { id: "w9-253-the-spotlight-fruit-moon", title: "The spotlight fruit moon", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Cal hung a banana beneath the spotlight to make a moon on stage. Ivy rehearsed her speech to the audience beneath its glow. Heat softened the fruit until it slipped from the hook. Ivy caught it with her tail and ate one bite without breaking her line. Cal dimmed the light. The play now had an eclipse. Afterward the audience praised the effect. Cal used a wooden moon for the next show, while Ivy packed a real banana to eat only after her speech." },
  { id: "w9-159-the-insurance-tree-branch", title: "The insurance tree branch", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Jade bought insurance for her banana tree against storms. Poe wrote the contract on a leaf. A wind tore the leaf away but left the tree intact. Jade claimed the policy had suffered storm damage. Poe denied it, saying the leaf was only paper. Jade climbed with her tail round a branch and fetched another leaf. She wrote a bill for his lost contract. Poe paid one banana to end the dispute and printed the next policy on cloth he could safely file indoors." },
  { id: "w9-165-the-efficient-complaint-chute", title: "The efficient complaint chute", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Pia built a chute for unhappy customers at the banana firm. Len called it efficient because every letter vanished at once. The business council praised the clear desks. Pia heard paper rustle under a tree and followed the chute with her tail. It emptied into the public garden. She gathered the letters and read one aloud at the next meeting. Len had sent it himself about the cold office. Pia closed the chute, fixed the heater, and hired Len to read mail." },
  { id: "w9-185-the-efficient-complaint-drum", title: "The efficient complaint drum", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Mina gave citizens a drum for protests about banana taxes. Sid praised the efficient system because he could hear it from his desk. Soon the whole town pounded it day and night. Sid wrapped the drum in blankets, but the sound shook his chair. Mina held the sticks in her tail and asked each citizen for one sentence. She wrote them on leaves for the committee. Sid read the leaves, lowered the tax, and returned the drum to the music school." },
  { id: "w9-199-the-insurance-umbrella-hole", title: "The insurance umbrella hole", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Dara claimed insurance for a torn umbrella at the banana stand. Len read her contract and said a hole let wind pass, reducing risk. Dara placed the umbrella above his desk. Rain fell through onto the policy pages. Len wrapped his tail round the papers and ran indoors. He approved the repair. Dara patched the cloth and offered him dry shelter. Len paid one banana for a seat. He rewrote the policy without the word hole and kept it away from the roof." },
  { id: "w9-212-the-ancient-chariot-brake", title: "The ancient chariot brake", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Lark drove an ancient chariot through the enormous arena. Dex carried bananas to feed the horses after the race. A dangerous bend sent the wheels sideways. Lark wrapped her tail round the rail and pulled a vine brake. The chariot stopped, but the horses kept going. Dex lured them back with fruit. Lark finished on foot with the chariot behind her. The crowd applauded the first safe stop it had seen. Dex sold brake vines outside the gate while the horses ate." },
  { id: "w9-252-the-orchestra-tail-bow", title: "The orchestra tail bow", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Bo led the orchestra with his tail as a bow. Nia placed the audience under the banana trees. Bo bowed low, and his tail struck the drum. The musicians took it as the opening beat. He stood, and the cymbals crashed. Bo stopped moving until Nia handed him a plain stick. The music settled into its proper tune. At the end he bowed again, but Nia held his tail behind the podium. The drummer still played one final note just in case." },
  { id: "w9-260-the-filmmaker-locked-script", title: "The filmmaker locked script", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Jade locked the film script in a banana crate. Poe, the filmmaker, lost the key before shooting. The actors waited in costumes. Jade hooked her tail through a gap and pulled out one page, but it held only the final line. Poe filmed that first. The actors invented scenes leading toward it while Jade fetched the spare key. When the crate opened, their version worked better. Poe kept the old script as scrap paper and paid the actors for writing the middle." },
  { id: "w9-155-the-mayor-stump-seat", title: "The mayor stump seat", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Fern ran for mayor on a promise of more seats. Hal counted votes beneath the banana tree. Fern won, then found the official chair was a stump. The committee had sold every other chair to pay for the election. Fern wrapped her tail round the stump and stood. She ordered the campaign signs cut into benches. Hal worried that the paint still praised her. Fern turned each sign face down. The town got seats, and no one had to sit on a promise." },
  { id: "w9-242-the-beautiful-rain-song", title: "The beautiful rain song", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Tess sang Cal a beautiful song beneath the banana trees. Cal leaned from a splendid window and listened. Rain filled the song box that played her backing tune. Tess lifted it with her tail, but the music slowed to a growl. Cal came down with a towel and sang the missing notes himself. They carried the box inside together. Tess kept the wet score as a reminder of their first duet. Cal dried it flat and wrote a simpler tune for weather they could not control." },
  { id: "w9-276-the-rehearsal-borrowed-beard", title: "The rehearsal borrowed beard", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo wore a long beard for rehearsal. Gus had made it from banana fibers for the costumes box. The tail of Cleo caught the beard during her royal bow, pulling it from her chin. The director demanded more glue. Gus shortened the beard instead. Cleo could bow safely, but the audience laughed at its uneven ends. She played a king who cut his own hair badly. Gus added a tiny wooden comb to the crown, and the laugh became part of the scene." },
  { id: "w9-203-the-secret-agent-peel-code", title: "The secret agent peel code", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Cal sent a secret code carved in a banana peel. Nia read it beneath an enormous bridge. Rain blurred the marks, making the message say bring chocolate instead of bring locks. Nia arrived at the vault with sweets in her tail. Cal frowned, but the guard opened the door to ask for a taste. Nia shared the box while Cal retrieved the stolen key. They locked the vault again. Cal wrote the next code on dry paper and added chocolate to their kit." },
  { id: "w9-229-the-ancient-map-rug", title: "The ancient map rug", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Fia marched an enormous army across an ancient map rug. Len moved the banana supply markers with his tail. The rug rolled up at one edge, trapping the enemy flag. Fia declared victory. Len unrolled it and showed the flag still there. The army had not left camp. A messenger brought a peace offer from the real enemy. Fia accepted before anyone had to walk. Len hung the rug on the wall, where no one could mistake a curled corner for conquered land." },
  { id: "w9-069-the-ghost-crew-wash-day", title: "The ghost crew wash day", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Ivy boarded a ghost ship to search for treasure. Reed carried a lantern in his tail. Pale shapes flapped along the deck and moaned about breakfast. Ivy touched one and found a wet sheet. The pirate crew had hung laundry on the ropes, then hidden below to scare guests away from their bananas. Reed raised his lantern and found red socks tangled among the pink sheets. Ivy offered soap in trade for fruit. The pirates accepted and asked her to keep their secret." },
  { id: "w9-186-the-business-nap-merger", title: "The business nap merger", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Nan merged her banana shop with Rex and his pillow stall. Their business promised fruit and rest in one place. The corporate office ordered every worker to nap while eating. Rex fell asleep with a banana in his tail. Nan woke him before it dropped. Customers waited beside empty tills. They split the hours into meals and naps. Sales recovered, but the office demanded a single product. Nan stuffed pillows with dry banana leaves. Rex sold them without asking anyone to chew." },
  { id: "w9-211-the-pirate-romantic-receipt", title: "The pirate romantic receipt", pay: 1600000, lib: 9, text: "Koa rescued Aya from a dangerous pirate boat. She demanded a receipt for the bananas he had thrown overboard to lighten it. Koa offered an enormous ruby as a token of love. Aya sold it at port and bought twice the fruit. He thought she had rejected him. She invited him aboard their repaired boat and showed two lunch baskets. Koa tied the mast rope with his tail. They sailed together, keeping all future love tokens small enough to fit beside the food." },
  { id: "w9-197-the-forecast-banana-hat", title: "The forecast banana hat", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Bea sold a forecast based on the angle of her banana hat. Rex bought it for his business council. The hat drooped, so she predicted falling sales. Rex stopped selling fruit and bought low shelves. Bea raised the hat with her tail and predicted growth. Rex raised the shelves again. A secretary asked for actual orders. Rex had sold none while moving shelves. He returned the forecast, put fruit at eye level, and sold Bea one fresh banana to hold up her hat." },
  { id: "w9-196-the-courtroom-missing-floor", title: "The courtroom missing floor", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Ari sued Nia for dropping bananas on his office floor. The courtroom heard testimony from the cleaner. Nia said the office had no floor because it stood on an open branch. Ari pointed to the ground far below. The judge asked whether his contract included the ground. Ari searched the page with his tail holding it steady. It covered one branch only. The judge dismissed the case and advised a basket. Ari bought one from Nia, who promised never to drop that." },
  { id: "w9-254-the-recording-soup-solo", title: "The recording soup solo", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Dex recorded Rose singing beside the banana kitchen. The recording picked up an enormous slurp from the cook. Dex tried to erase it, but it matched the beat. Rose used her tail to tap the rhythm on a pot and sang again. The audience bought the song as soup jazz. The cook asked for a credit. Dex printed his name on the record sleeve. Rose kept the pot in the studio, and the cook learned to slurp only when the red lamp glowed." },
  { id: "w9-172-the-corporate-ladder-roots", title: "The corporate ladder roots", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Zia climbed the corporate ladder in a banana tree. Lou had nailed it to the trunk for the official promotion race. At the top Zia found a sign reading chief of roots. She climbed down, tail sore, and asked where the office stood. Lou pointed beneath the soil. Zia dug a room beside the roots and sold cool drinks to passing workers. Lou demanded a share because he owned the ladder. Zia showed him the root sign and hired him to serve below the roots." },
  { id: "w9-227-the-action-cape-turnstile", title: "The action cape turnstile", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Dara chased a dangerous robber in her splendid hero cape. Hal operated the market turnstile. The cape caught while Dara swung over the gate with her tail. The robber escaped, but his stolen banana basket caught the cape too. Hal turned the gate backward and freed both. Dara returned the basket to the vendor. She shortened the cape before the next chase. Hal kept its spare cloth as a flag to warn heroes where the gate stood, even when they insisted on leaping." },
  { id: "w9-269-the-composer-silent-bell", title: "The composer silent bell", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Tess wrote a song for a bell with no clapper. Len, the musician, waited beneath the banana tree. He shook the bell, producing nothing. Tess called the silence planned. A goat rang its neck bell nearby and spoiled the pause. Len caught the silent bell in his tail and moved the concert indoors. The audience sat quietly for one minute, then asked for a tune. Tess put a clapper inside and wrote one. Len played it outside, where the goat joined only after the final note." },
  { id: "w9-086-the-pirate-apology-flag", title: "The pirate apology flag", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Lark raised a splendid black flag above her boat. Joss had washed it with a red shirt, so it turned pink. Their dangerous rivals laughed from the dock. Lark tried to lower it with her tail, but the rope snapped. Joss wrote sorry on the flag in banana paste. The rivals came aboard to ask what she meant. Lark said she was sorry for taking their soup pot last week. They accepted the pot back and stayed for soup beneath the pink flag." },
  { id: "w9-188-the-inventory-loan-banana", title: "The inventory loan banana", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Pia loaned Len a banana to improve his inventory count. Len loaned it back to improve hers. Their business reports showed two full shelves while one fruit traveled between them. An auditor watched Pia swing it across the lane with her tail. He asked who could eat it. Neither wanted to ruin the count. The auditor split it in half and recorded one meal shared. Pia and Len closed the false shelves. Their next reports listed one empty plate and no debt." },
  { id: "w9-273-the-spotlight-empty-throne", title: "The spotlight empty throne", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Zia aimed the spotlight at the royal throne. Sid, the director, ordered the actor to stand far away for a lonely scene. The audience could see only the empty chair. Sid whispered for more emotion. Zia used her tail to turn the lamp toward the actor instead. His face told the scene clearly. Sid moved the throne beside him for the final line. Zia marked both places with chalk, so the next lonely king would still have enough light to be seen." },
  { id: "w9-051-the-spaceship-banana-rack", title: "The spaceship banana rack", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Orla strapped bananas to the spaceship wall. Dex forgot to strap himself. When the engine stopped, he floated past the splendid rack and grabbed fruit with his tail. Each banana sent him spinning faster. Orla caught his belt with a long hook. She tied him beside the rack until the ship landed. The moon guard asked what cargo they carried. Dex said fresh fruit and one bruised pilot. Orla sold the guard a bunch and kept Dex tied down until the hatch opened." },
  { id: "w9-247-the-secret-agent-glue-glove", title: "The secret agent glue glove", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Ari wore a dangerous glue glove to climb the enemy wall. Nia waited below with an enormous banana cart. The glove stuck to the wall, and Ari could not move. Nia looped her tail round his boot and passed up warm water. Ari washed the glue free but slipped toward the cart. Nia caught him in the soft fruit. They returned with no secrets and a lot of mash. Ari sold the glove recipe to a furniture shop, where sticking in place was useful." },
  { id: "w9-119-the-baseball-shadow-catch", title: "The baseball shadow catch", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Toma chased a baseball across an enormous field. Jade shouted that he was following its shadow. He stopped beneath a banana tree and held his tail out. He caught the ball in his curled tail while its shadow slid away. Jade called the catch splendid. A dangerous wind sent the next hit toward the pond. Toma watched the shadow again but kept his eyes up. He caught the ball before it splashed. Jade painted a sun on his glove to remind him where to look." },
  { id: "w9-174-the-efficient-tax-basket", title: "The efficient tax basket", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Bea taxed every banana entering the village. Sid built an enormous basket to speed the count. Bea called it efficient and jumped inside to stamp each fruit with her tail. Traders began bringing empty peels. Sid counted them as bananas under the official rule. Bea opened the basket and found no tax meal. She changed the rule to edible fruit. Sid ate one to test it and had to pay. Bea kept him at the desk with his lunch sealed outside." },
  { id: "w9-175-the-insurance-rain-umbrella", title: "The insurance rain umbrella", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo bought insurance against rain at her banana stall. Tom sold umbrellas beside her. When clouds gathered, he covered her roof for free. The stall stayed dry, so her claim failed. Cleo accused him of stealing her payout. Tom offered an umbrella sales fee instead. She sold six before the storm ended. Her business earned more than the claim. Cleo renewed the policy for wind, then tied every umbrella handle to the counter with her tail while Tom held the roof." },
  { id: "w9-243-the-historical-royal-shoes", title: "The historical royal shoes", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Uma sewed enormous shoes for the royal parade. Hal wore them to seem taller than the visiting prince. A messenger warned that the banana gate stood low. Hal ducked, caught a shoe on a root, and fell into the arms of Uma. She used her tail to untie the tall soles. The prince bowed to Hal at his real height. Uma sold the removed blocks as foot rests. Hal kept plain shoes for the next parade and hired Uma to measure gates before crowns." },
  { id: "w9-195-the-secretary-double-lunch", title: "The secretary double lunch", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Zia booked two clients for lunch with Gus at the banana firm. Her secretary chart showed two empty hours, but they were the same hour on different pages. Gus used his tail to hold both soup bowls and asked the clients to share a table. They found they sold the same crates and argued over the business contract. Zia brought one common order sheet. Gus bought half from each. She fixed the chart, then booked herself a single quiet lunch with no crates." },
  { id: "w9-220-the-anniversary-tree-ring", title: "The anniversary tree ring", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Uma asked Poe for a yearly ring. He counted tree rings in the banana grove and brought an enormous stump. Uma used her tail to roll it onto the porch. It blocked the door. Poe offered to carve it smaller, but she noticed the smooth top made a fine table. They ate pineapple there and marked one ring for each year together. Poe carved a tiny ring from the spare wood. Uma wore it and kept the table for gifts that needed more room." },
  { id: "w9-238-the-action-hero-cloak-rack", title: "The action hero cloak rack", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Orla hung her hero cloak in the banana cafe. Hal took it for a splendid table cover and set dinner on it. A dangerous call for help came from the grove. Orla pulled the cloak with her tail, spilling soup, then raced outside. Hal followed with a clean sheet. She rescued a monkey from a broken branch and used the sheet as a sling. Orla left her cloak at home next time. Hal kept the sheet near the door, where useful cloth mattered more than a secret costume." },
  { id: "w9-246-the-historical-dinner-trumpet", title: "The historical dinner trumpet", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Zia sounded the royal trumpet for an enormous feast. Dex waited to carry banana soup into the hall. A messenger slipped him the wrong signal card. He entered during the war anthem. The generals stood and saluted the soup. Zia caught the card with her tail and stopped playing. Dex served them before telling them of the error. They agreed to discuss peace after lunch. Zia wrote a clearer card for dinner and kept every anthem in a separate box far from the kitchen." },
  { id: "w9-258-the-sleeping-star-hammock", title: "The sleeping star hammock", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Hope booked a superstar for the banana festival. Hal built an enormous hammock backstage. The audience waited while the star slept. Hope rocked the hammock with her tail to wake him, but the gentle motion deepened his nap. Hal carried it onto the stage. The audience watched the sleeping star in silence, then clapped when he snored. Hope sold tickets as a quiet rest show. Hal lowered the hammock after one hour. The star woke, took a banana, and thanked them for a good set." },
  { id: "w9-248-the-romantic-apology-bench", title: "The romantic apology bench", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Bea promised Gus a beautiful apology after missing dinner. She carved a splendid bench in the banana grove and wrote sorry across its seat. Gus sat before the paint dried. Bea wiped his coat with her tail, making the stain wider. He laughed and asked for dinner instead. They ate on the ground while the bench dried. Bea repainted the word on a sign above it, where no coat could touch. Gus used the bench next day and found a meal basket waiting beneath it." },
  { id: "w9-278-the-superstar-quiet-costume", title: "The superstar quiet costume", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Esme hid a superstar in a gardener costume. Tom led him through the audience after the banana concert. The star bowed to everyone, giving himself away. Esme held his sleeve with her tail and handed him a watering can. He watered the flowers instead of posing. Fans asked the gardener for help with their plants. The star gave plain advice and reached the gate safely. Tom booked a garden tour for the next day, but Esme warned him to leave all stage bows at home." },
  { id: "w9-215-the-historical-banana-mint", title: "The historical banana mint", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Orla minted coins shaped like bananas for the king. Bo counted the enormous royal treasure. A messenger reported that hungry citizens had bitten every coin. Orla used her tail to hold one beside a real banana and saw the problem. She punched a hole through each new coin so it looked less like fruit. Bo strung them on vines. Citizens stopped biting them and bought food instead. The king said his coins looked cheap. Orla showed him the tooth marks on the old gold." },
  { id: "w9-236-the-romantic-train-basket", title: "The romantic train basket", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Mina ran beside a train with a beautiful banana basket for Gil. He reached out, but her tail caught the platform rail. The basket landed in an enormous mail cart. Gil jumped off before leaving and helped her free it. Mina thought she had ruined his grand journey. He had only bought a ticket to deliver her birthday cake from the next town. They opened both baskets on the bench. The train left, carrying one empty cake box the porter had mistaken for luggage." },
  { id: "w9-240-the-historical-border-picnic", title: "The historical border picnic", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Rose drew an ancient border between two banana kingdoms. Dex placed an enormous stone on the line. A messenger arrived with a treaty saying the stone must be shared. Neither kingdom could lift half of it. Rose wrapped her tail round a vine and tested its weight. Dex brought lunch while she thought. They spread a cloth over the stone and sat on opposite sides. The treaty became a picnic pact. The stone stayed whole, and both kings learned to pass the fruit bowl across it." },
  { id: "w9-271-the-broadcast-banana-poll", title: "The broadcast banana poll", pay: 1620000, lib: 9, text: "Vera asked the broadcast audience to vote for their favorite fruit. Rex, the director, counted banana peels mailed to the studio. One grower sent an enormous sack. Vera held it in her tail and noticed every peel came from the same bunch. Rex wanted to count all votes. Vera limited each sender to one reply. Bananas still won, but by less. The grower got his sack back with a note asking him to sell fruit instead of mailing breakfast waste to a camera." },
  { id: "w9-245-the-beautiful-rival-map", title: "The beautiful rival map", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Wren and Bo both loved a beautiful map maker. Wren brought an enormous pearl. Bo brought a banana and a compass. The map maker asked them to mark a new path through the grove. The pearl from Wren rolled down the hill, and her tail caught it beside a hidden spring. Bo used his compass to chart the spring. The map maker thanked both and married neither. Wren kept the pearl, Bo ate the banana, and the new path let them visit each other without getting lost." },
  { id: "w9-206-the-action-hero-soap-rope", title: "The action hero soap rope", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Fern hung above a dangerous pit on a rope. Tom stood on the splendid ledge with the stolen banana chest. Fern caught the rope with her tail and tried to climb, but it slid through her hands. Tom had washed it with soap to remove his prints. Fern swung toward a dry root instead. She climbed out and rubbed the soapy rope over the chest. It slipped from the hands of Tom. Fern caught the chest, returned the fruit, and sent Tom a bill for soap." },
  { id: "w9-190-the-testimony-tail-curtain", title: "The testimony tail curtain", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Sia built a curtain behind the courtroom witness seat. Tom said it would make testimony seem serious. Sia pulled it open with her tail to reveal the witness and his banana snack. The audience clapped. The judge ordered silence. Tom lowered the curtain at the wrong moment, hiding the witness before his answer. Sia took the rope away and left the curtain open. The witness answered plainly. Tom got a job at the theater, where his official duty was waiting for the final line." },
  { id: "w9-285-the-cinematic-tiny-giant", title: "The cinematic tiny giant", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Lark filmed a cinematic giant among tiny banana houses. Hal, the director, knelt in the set with his tail behind the painted hills. The audience test laughed because his ears touched the cardboard sky. Lark moved the camera lower and cropped the ears. Hal looked enormous at last. He sneezed and flattened three houses. Lark filmed the sneeze as the final mistake of the giant. Hal rebuilt the houses after shooting and kept his nose behind the hills during every later close view." },
  { id: "w9-115-the-detective-sugar-glove", title: "The detective sugar glove", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Otis found sugar on a splendid glove where the missing banana tart had stood. Aya offered to help the detective. Otis sniffed each monkey hand, finding no sugar. Aya used her tail to lift the glove. It had stretched wide, with a heel mark inside. Someone had worn it on a foot. They followed sweet tracks to the cook, who had stepped on sugar while carrying the tart to cool outside. Otis returned the glove. Aya washed the porch and got the first cooled slice." },
  { id: "w9-192-the-contract-rain-signature", title: "The contract rain signature", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Uma signed a contract on a banana leaf during rain. Kip watched the ink wash away. The ownership dispute returned at once. Uma claimed the tree, and Kip claimed the ground. They stood beneath it with their tails linked to stop another wet sheet escaping. A gardener offered to plant a new tree on the ground owned by Kip. Uma kept the old one. They signed on dry bark indoors. The gardener took the leaf home, where he added it to the compost beneath his roses." },
  { id: "w9-268-the-superstar-autograph-peel", title: "The superstar autograph peel", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Sia sold banana peels signed by a superstar. Cal waited in the audience line for one. The ink ran as the peel browned. Sia tried drying it with her tail fanning the air, but the signature cracked. Cal asked for plain paper instead. Sia printed a note saying the star had eaten this banana. The star laughed and signed both note and paper. Cal kept the paper, ate his own banana, and used the peel as compost without expecting a name to last in soil." },
  { id: "w9-297-the-animation-banana-frame", title: "The animation banana frame", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Ari finished an animation about a banana boat. Tom, the director, wanted an enormous frame around it for the festival. Ari used her tail to carry a wooden frame to the screen. It blocked half the picture. Tom meant a title frame inside the film, not wood outside. Ari added one with the boat name and took the wood home. The audience saw the whole voyage. Tom helped turn the spare frame into a window for the studio of Ari, where it finally showed a useful view." },
  { id: "w9-156-the-inventory-tail-stamp", title: "The inventory tail stamp", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Gil counted inventory in the banana store. Rue stamped each crate for the business audit. Gil dipped his tail in ink to work faster. He swung past five crates and marked them twice. Rue found twice as much fruit on paper as on the shelves. Gil proposed selling the paper surplus. Rue handed him a cloth and made him erase each spare mark. He counted again with his hands. The audit passed, and the cloth became the only stock they could honestly add." },
  { id: "w9-187-the-campaign-root-tour", title: "The campaign root tour", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Orla toured the banana farms for her campaign. Gus carried the official camera. Orla posed with clean boots beside an enormous root. A farmer asked her to lift a water bucket. She wrapped her tail round its handle and slipped in mud. Gus lowered the camera. Orla told him to take the picture anyway. She finished watering the row and washed her boots after. The committee photo won votes because the bucket had reached the trees, even if the mayor had sat in mud." },
  { id: "w9-244-the-dangerous-catapult-picnic", title: "The dangerous catapult picnic", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Vera loaded a dangerous catapult with an enormous banana basket. Sid planned to launch her over the wall with it. Vera curled her tail round the frame and refused until he tested the basket alone. It sailed over and landed in the royal feast. Guests cheered for fresh fruit. Sid launched a note asking for the gate to open. Vera walked through with the empty sling in her hands. The king hired them to bring fruit but insisted that all workers use the door." },
  { id: "w9-267-the-animation-tree-roots", title: "The animation tree roots", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Rose drew a banana tree for an animation. Hal moved its leaves in each frame. The roots wandered too, making the tree chase the actors. Rose asked the director to stop the drift. Hal used his tail to pin the root guide beneath the paper. The tree stood still, but its moving leaves still looked hungry. Rose wrote a scene where it caught a falling monkey. Hal kept the playful leaves. The finished film gave the tree one useful rescue and a firm place to stand." },
  { id: "w9-288-the-superstar-stage-fruit", title: "The superstar stage fruit", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Orla booked a superstar who demanded only green bananas. Gus bought an enormous crate, then the fruit ripened before the show. Orla painted one peel green, but the star spotted her stained tail. Gus offered the ripe fruit plainly. The star tasted one and liked it. The audience got the rest at the break. Orla erased green from the contract and wrote fresh instead. Gus planted the painted peel in compost far from the food table, where color no longer counted as flavor." },
  { id: "w9-290-the-filmmaker-midnight-sun", title: "The filmmaker midnight sun", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Rose scheduled a sunrise scene for midnight. Poe, the filmmaker, wanted to shoot before the banana market opened. The director lit an enormous lamp behind a painted hill. Rose used her tail to move the sunrise slowly, but a real owl crossed the frame. Poe called it proof of dawn. Rose added a rooster sound after filming. The audience believed the scene. Poe credited the owl as night watch, while Rose booked the next real sunrise early enough to get it before the fruit carts arrived." },
  { id: "w9-171-the-boardroom-banana-bell", title: "The boardroom banana bell", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Wren rang a boardroom bell whenever someone had a useful idea. Kip proposed longer meetings to hear more ideas. Wren rang the bell. No one could hear the next speaker. Kip wrapped his tail round its clapper and waited. The business council stared in silence until the banana cart arrived. Everyone spoke at once about lunch. Wren removed the bell and wrote each idea on paper. Kip got one approved meeting rule. Lunch came before the talk, and the bell called only the cart." },
  { id: "w9-200-the-committee-final-basket", title: "The committee final basket", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Esme chaired the committee for banana waste. Tom brought an enormous empty basket as a proposal. They discussed its shape until ripe fruit spoiled outside. Esme carried the basket with her tail into the grove and filled it. Tom opened the gate for hungry neighbors. Every banana went. The committee asked for minutes proving the plan. Esme set the empty basket on the table. Tom wrote one sentence stating that the fruit had been eaten. They closed the meeting before another bunch fell." },
  { id: "w9-205-the-ancient-king-nightshirt", title: "The ancient king nightshirt", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Etta smuggled Sid from the palace in an ancient king costume. His enormous crown caught the door, and his tail tangled in the cape. Guards hurried toward them. Etta stripped off the costume, leaving Sid in his sleep shirt. A messenger asked why the laundry boy had royal clothes. Etta gave him the bundle and said it needed washing. The guards carried it away. Sid escaped through the banana garden, where Etta charged him one crown coin for repairing her torn disguise bag." },
  { id: "w9-219-the-secret-tunnel-echo-hat", title: "The secret tunnel echo hat", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Tess escaped through a secret tunnel with proof that Len had stolen banana funds. Len chased the sound of her boots. Tess hung a splendid hat beside an echo hole and flicked it with her tail. The sound drew Len down a dangerous side path. He reached a dry well and found only his own echo. Tess left the records at the court, then returned with a rope. Len climbed out and paid her for the rescue. She took back her hat, which he had stolen too." },
  { id: "w9-193-the-corporate-brand-tail", title: "The corporate brand tail", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Vera painted the tail of every worker gold for the corporate banana brand. Hal objected that paint made his tail slip from branches. The business office offered gloves, which fit hands but not tails. Vera watched him fall into a soft crate. She washed the paint off with her own tail holding the cloth. Hal climbed safely again. Vera put the gold on crate labels instead. The office claimed a new brand vision. Hal asked for a label on his glove box reading not needed." },
  { id: "w9-226-the-historical-clock-march", title: "The historical clock march", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo ordered an enormous march at sunrise. Rex wound the ancient clock before serving bananas. It rang at midnight, waking every soldier. Cleo marched them across the yard, then saw the stars. She wrapped her tail round the bell cord to stop it. Rex found a mouse nest holding the hour hand back. They moved the nest to a box and let the troops sleep. At real sunrise the clock rang once. Cleo held the parade after breakfast and kept a window beside the dial." },
  { id: "w9-235-the-ancient-banquet-menu", title: "The ancient banquet menu", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Lark restored an ancient banquet for the enormous royal birthday. Sid read the menu in a new tongue. It called for banana leaves, which Lark cooked into a bitter stew. A messenger found the next line, which said use them as plates. Lark poured the stew into a garden pot and served fresh fruit on new leaves. Sid edited the menu while holding it steady with his tail. The king praised the old recipe. Lark showed him the full page before anyone asked for more stew." },
  { id: "w9-216-the-chase-scene-nap-cart", title: "The chase scene nap cart", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Pia chased a dangerous thief through the banana market. Cal drove an enormous nap cart across her path. She leaped onto it, tail wrapped round the rail, and bounced off a pillow toward the thief. He stopped to catch his stolen hat. Pia caught him and returned the hat to its owner. Cal billed the town for one crushed pillow. Pia paid from the reward. She kept the pillow in her chase kit, where its soft corner proved more useful than another hard helmet." },
  { id: "w9-293-the-spotlight-paper-hero", title: "The spotlight paper hero", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Uma played a hero beneath the spotlight. Rex built an enormous dragon from banana crates and paper. Its head fell forward before the battle. Uma caught it with her tail and called the dragon tired. The audience laughed as she helped it sit. Rex moved the hidden strings to let it bow. Uma offered it a wooden fruit instead of drawing her sword. The director kept the new ending. Rex braced the neck after the show so kindness would not depend on a broken hinge." },
  { id: "w9-117-the-chess-king-umbrella", title: "The chess king umbrella", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Rex entered a chess contest under the banana trees. Sia brought an enormous umbrella because the sky looked dangerous. Rain began as Rex moved his king. Sia tilted the umbrella with her tail and struck the table, sliding every piece across the board. Rex lost his winning move. The judge set up the last known position, but no one agreed where the pawns belonged. Sia used leaves to draw it from memory. Rex won, then bought a board with small holes for each piece." },
  { id: "w9-261-the-broadcast-rain-window", title: "The broadcast rain window", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Koa forecast rain on the broadcast news. Meg, the director, sprayed the window to give him proof. Koa used his tail to wipe a clear patch and saw sunshine. He told viewers to check their own windows. Meg stopped spraying and moved the camera outside the banana grove. Real clouds arrived by the next hour. Koa reported them without a hose. Meg kept the sprayer for plants and put the forecast desk far enough away that no wet glass could pretend to be a sky." },
  { id: "w9-295-the-cinematic-golden-lunch", title: "The cinematic golden lunch", pay: 1640000, lib: 9, text: "Wren made the cinematic sunset gold by painting the banana set yellow. Sid, the director, painted the lunch bowls too. Actors refused to eat from wet paint. Wren caught a bowl with her tail and saw the mistake. She moved real lunch off set and used wooden food for the scene. The audience admired the golden feast. Sid ate plain bananas behind the camera. Wren kept separate signs for props and meals, so no new color plan could turn dinner into scenery again." },
  { id: "w9-234-the-action-alarm-banana", title: "The action alarm banana", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Koa guarded an enormous banana vault with a dangerous alarm. Rex tossed a peel over the beam to test it. The bell rang, and Koa ran outside while Rex stayed beside the fruit. Koa realized her mistake and returned with her tail round the door handle. Rex offered the test receipt. Koa changed the alarm to lock the door before ringing. During the next test Rex got trapped inside with no fruit key. Koa let him out after he paid for the banana he ate." },
  { id: "w9-157-the-warranty-rain-desk", title: "The warranty rain desk", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Hope bought a desk with a lifetime warranty. Len placed it in the banana grove for meetings. Rain dissolved its glue, and the drawers fell onto his tail. Hope took the contract to the seller. The seller said lifetime meant the life of the desk, which had ended. Hope set the loose drawers on his counter and asked him to certify the death. He refused to sign. She returned the next day with a working desk rebuilt from the drawers and claimed the warranty lived too." },
  { id: "w9-228-the-love-potion-soup-ladle", title: "The love potion soup ladle", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Esme bought a beautiful love potion for Cal. The cook poured it into the enormous banana soup pot by mistake. Every guest praised the soup and hugged the ladle. Esme lifted it with her tail, and the crowd followed her to the sink. Cal brought plain water and washed the ladle. The spell faded. He asked Esme to supper without any potion. She accepted. The cook kept the empty bottle to hold salt and locked the soup recipe well away from the magic shelf." },
  { id: "w9-272-the-orchestra-wind-fan", title: "The orchestra wind fan", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Wren set a fan beside the orchestra to keep musicians cool. Cal arranged the audience under banana leaves. The fan blew sheet music into the trees. Wren caught one page with her tail and played its last bar over and over. Cal fetched the rest with a ladder. The audience hummed the repeating tune until the song returned. Wren turned the fan toward the empty wall. Cal clipped each page to its stand and charged no one for the extra verse the wind had written." },
  { id: "w9-209-the-hover-ship-tail-basket", title: "The hover ship tail basket", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Ira flew a hover ship above the enormous banana grove. Meg hung from its rescue basket with her tail through the mesh. The pilot tried to lift a trapped worker, but the basket held too much fruit. Ira ordered Meg to dump the bananas. She passed them to the worker first, then cleared the basket. A dangerous branch broke as the lift rose. Meg caught its vine and steadied them. They landed with one worker holding the saved fruit, and he shared his bunch with them." },
  { id: "w9-266-the-rehearsal-ghost-blanket", title: "The rehearsal ghost blanket", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Pia played a ghost during rehearsal. Tom washed the costumes beside the banana stage. Her blanket shrank, leaving her tail bare. The director wanted a spooky entrance, but the tail made the audience laugh. Pia used it to lift a chair without showing her hands. Tom added a plain sheet to the blanket. Pia kept the tail trick beneath it. The show scared no one, but every child asked how the chair floated. Tom sold the answer as a lesson in hidden tail tricks after the curtain fell." },
  { id: "w9-279-the-composer-rain-bucket", title: "The composer rain bucket", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Fia wrote a song using rain on banana leaves. Poe, the musician, set buckets beneath each leaf to deepen the notes. An enormous storm filled them before the audience arrived. Fia tipped one with her tail and spilled water over the stage. Poe emptied the buckets into the garden and moved the show beneath a roof. They tapped dry leaves with small sticks. Poe made a recording before rain drowned their tapping. Fia wrote the garden watering into the setup sheet, far from the actual score." },
  { id: "w9-274-the-recording-banana-mute", title: "The recording banana mute", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Ari recorded Bo playing a banana leaf flute. The recording stayed silent though the cheeks of the musician puffed red. Ari checked the wire with her tail and found the mute switch beneath his lunch basket. Bo moved it, but the leaf had dried and cracked. Ari handed him a fresh leaf from the grove. The tune returned. Bo played one short song before the next leaf dried. Ari saved that take and put lunch on a separate shelf, where no sandwich could silence the music." },
  { id: "w9-241-the-secret-agent-fruit-scale", title: "The secret agent fruit scale", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Sia met a dangerous agent at the banana stall. Rex weighed fruit to hide their secret exchange. Sia set a splendid envelope on the scale. Rex put a banana beside it, but the needle rose too far. The envelope held a gold key, not paper. Sia curled her tail round it before a customer saw. Rex demanded payment for the fruit used as cover. She gave him the banana. He kept the peel as a receipt, then sold the scale because he no longer knew what a normal sale weighed." },
  { id: "w9-249-the-ancient-statue-hat", title: "The ancient statue hat", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Cleo built an enormous statue of an ancient king. Rex added a banana crown to show his wealth. A messenger warned that birds would eat it. Cleo climbed with her tail round the stone arm and replaced the crown with carved fruit. The birds nested inside the hollow hat instead. Rex wanted them removed before the unveiling. Cleo cut a small door in the back for cleaning. The town praised the king for giving birds a home, which was kinder than anything he had done in life." },
  { id: "w9-296-the-rehearsal-missing-king", title: "The rehearsal missing king", pay: 1660000, lib: 9, text: "Zia waited for the king actor at rehearsal. Gus stood in the costumes room with an enormous crown stuck over his eyes. Zia pulled it free with her tail. He could see, but the crown no longer fit. The director gave him a paper crown and let the heavy one sit on the throne. The audience accepted both symbols. Gus finished his lines without a stumble. Zia measured every hat after the show and wrote actor size beside each role, above the banana lunch list." },
  { id: "w9-225-the-beautiful-castle-letterbox", title: "The beautiful castle letterbox", pay: 1680000, lib: 9, text: "Bea waited for Sid and his beautiful love letters. Each morning her splendid castle box held banana peels instead. She climbed inside with her tail round the lid and found letters wedged in the back. Sid had fed the palace pet through the same slot. Bea read the letters, then wrote one asking for two boxes. Sid built them side by side and painted hearts on hers. The pet learned to open only the fruit lid. Bea finally got dry letters and a quiet morning." },
  { id: "w9-281-the-broadcast-silent-guest", title: "The broadcast silent guest", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Hope invited Nia to the broadcast banana show. The director told Nia to answer briefly. Hope asked about her enormous garden. Nia nodded. Hope asked about her harvest. Nia nodded again. Hope wrapped her tail round the cue card and read the card text aloud. Nia thought briefly meant no words. She finally described the garden, and viewers learned how to grow fruit. Hope changed the card to short answers welcome. Nia returned next week with a banana and a story, both small enough for the show." },
  { id: "w9-289-the-composer-borrowed-hum", title: "The composer borrowed hum", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Pia heard Tom humming beside the banana grove and wrote the tune for her orchestra. Tom, a gardener, heard his tune at the concert. Pia called it an original song. Tom hummed the last bar before the musicians reached it. The audience noticed. Pia lowered her tail baton and named him as composer. Tom said his grandma had taught it to him. Pia credited the family tune and kept her new score. Tom came to the next show with grandma and two seats they had earned." },
  { id: "w9-291-the-broadcast-guest-tail", title: "The broadcast guest tail", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Sia spoke with Bo on the broadcast banana hour. The director asked for no movement in the shot. Bo wrapped his tail round the chair leg and answered calmly. Sia tried to shift the chair closer to the camera. Bo moved with it and knocked the enormous fruit bowl over. The director stopped filming. Sia untied the tail and gave Bo a chair with arms. He held those instead. The interview resumed without spills, though Sia let the first question be why tails needed room too." },
  { id: "w9-178-the-courtroom-echo-witness", title: "The courtroom echo witness", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Fia accused Rex of taking her bananas. The courtroom stood beneath an enormous echo arch. Each charge sounded twice, and the judge called this strong testimony. Rex shouted no, which echoed too. Fia wrapped her tail round a curtain rope and drew cloth across the arch. The echo stopped. Rex showed the fruit receipt from her own shop. Fia had lost track of his order. She withdrew the charge. The judge kept the curtain and billed the arch owner for making every trial twice as long." },
  { id: "w9-221-the-waterfall-chase-ferry", title: "The waterfall chase ferry", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Vera fled a dangerous chase toward a waterfall. Dex waited with an enormous ferry full of bananas. She landed aboard, tail hooked round a rope. The pursuers stopped at the bank because the ferry charged a fare. Dex offered them a group rate. Vera paid him double to leave at once. He took both offers and crossed with everyone. At the far bank Vera showed the court order clearing her name. Dex returned the fare to the pursuers in bananas and kept the fee from Vera for the quick ride." },
  { id: "w9-237-the-dangerous-royal-portrait", title: "The dangerous royal portrait", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Nan painted an enormous royal portrait. Cal stood guard because a dangerous rival wanted to steal the image of the king. Nan saw a shadow slip through the banana window. She caught its sleeve with her tail. The visitor carried a tiny brush and claimed to be the king. Cal checked his face against the half done portrait. Nan had painted the nose wrong. The king fixed it himself, then paid her. Cal guarded the finished portrait and asked Nan to paint visitors only after checking their names." },
  { id: "w9-298-the-superstar-home-encore", title: "The superstar home encore", pay: 1700000, lib: 9, text: "Bea called for the superstar encore after the banana concert. Hal had already packed the sound box and gone home. The audience clapped longer. Bea followed his tracks with her tail carrying the stage lamp. Hal sat at his kitchen table, eating an enormous supper. Bea asked for one more song. He sang quietly while washing his bowl. She recorded it with his consent and played it outside the hall. The audience left satisfied, and Hal finished supper without putting his stage coat back on." },
  { id: "w9-300-the-filmmaker-closing-door", title: "The filmmaker closing door", pay: 1720000, lib: 9, text: "Dara filmed the final scene at a banana cafe. Rex, the filmmaker, wanted the hero to close the door as the audience heard music. The tail of the hero held the handle too tightly, pulling the whole door from its enormous hinge. Dara stopped the camera. Rex laughed and wanted to keep the crash. Dara repaired the door first, then filmed a gentle close. She used the crash after the credits as a rehearsal outtake. The cafe reopened next morning, with its door working and no actor blocking breakfast." },
  { id: "w9-224-the-samurai-banana-sheath", title: "The samurai banana sheath", pay: 1720000, lib: 9, text: "Ari faced Poe in a dangerous duel beneath an enormous banana tree. Ari reached for his sword, but the sheath held only fruit. The cook had swapped it for a lunch tube. Poe laughed and lowered his blade. Ari peeled the banana with his tail and offered half. Poe accepted, then admitted his sword was wooden. They had both come to look brave rather than fight. The cook fetched the real sword to cut bread. Ari carried the fruit sheath home and left the blade in the kitchen." },
  { id: "w9-223-the-chocolate-coded-kiss", title: "The chocolate coded kiss", pay: 1720000, lib: 9, text: "Zia sent Bo a chocolate kiss with a secret message inside. He ate the message with the sweet. The dangerous meeting place vanished from memory. Zia waited at the banana dock with her tail round an enormous rope. Bo visited every sweet shop until he found the wrapper printer. The printer recalled the message and sent him to the dock. He arrived late with a fresh box. Zia made him read every wrapper before eating. Their next message came on a plain card too large to fit in his mouth." },
  { id: "w9-270-the-filmmaker-fruit-credits", title: "The filmmaker fruit credits", pay: 1720000, lib: 9, text: "Uma listed every helper in the film credits. Poe, the filmmaker, wanted to credit each banana eaten on set too. The names filled an enormous paper roll. Uma held it with her tail while the audience waited for the lights. Poe insisted the fruit had powered the acting. Uma wrote one line thanking the banana growers and rolled up the rest. The audience clapped and left before midnight. Poe kept the unused roll to write the next script, which had enough pages without naming his lunch." },
  { id: "w9-180-the-ownership-vine-invoice", title: "The ownership vine invoice", pay: 1740000, lib: 9, text: "Hugo claimed ownership of the knot he used to hang bananas. Nia tied the same knot in a tree swing. Hugo sent a contract demanding payment for each twist. Nia untied the swing and held its ends in her tail. She charged him for testing his knot. Hugo refused. Nia let go of the loose ends. The swing fell, spilling his lunch basket. Nia offered to tie it back for one banana. Hugo paid, then crossed out his invoice. The knot kept its shape, and they kept their coins." },
  { id: "w9-250-the-dangerous-finale-rope", title: "The dangerous finale rope", pay: 1760000, lib: 9, text: "Dara reached the dangerous end of her chase on an enormous rope bridge. Tom held the stolen banana chest on the far bank. She swung beneath the bridge by her tail and cut his escape rope. He could still walk home, so he shrugged. Dara realized the theft had no grand finale. She showed him the court order and opened the chest. Tom returned every bunch. Dara found a short path around the gorge and moved the bridge ropes to mark it. Tom carried the posts under her watch." }
);
